<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="PRO" style="id">EN_UST en_English_ltr Mon Apr 29 2024 14:15:26 GMT-0700 (Pacific Daylight Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Proverbs
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Proverbs
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Proverbs
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Pro
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Proverbs

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PRO 1"/>
  <para style="m"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 1:1"/>{These are} the wise sayings said by Solomon. {He was} David’s son and Israel’s king.
<verse eid="PRO 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 1:2"/>{These wise sayings are} for knowing what is wise and instructive.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They are} for understanding insightful things that people say.
<verse eid="PRO 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 1:3"/>{These wise sayings are} for instructing someone about what is insightful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">righteous, just, and honest.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 1:4"/>{They are} for making naive people prudent,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {for making} young people knowledgeable and discreet.
<verse eid="PRO 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 1:5"/>(Let wise people listen {to these wise sayings} and learn more.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {let these sayings} guide understanding people so that they know what to do.)
<verse eid="PRO 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 1:6"/>{These wise sayings are} for understanding wise sayings and parables.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Indeed, they are for understanding} what wise people say and the riddles they tell.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 1:7"/>In order to become knowledgeable, a person must begin by deeply respecting Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{But} foolish people detest what is wise or instructive.

<verse eid="PRO 1:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 1:8"/>My child, listen carefully to what I, your father, am teaching you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, obey the rules that your mother has commanded.
<verse eid="PRO 1:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 1:9"/>{Obey your parents’ teaching} because then {people will admire and respect you;} it will be as if those teachings were an attractive wreath on your head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or beautiful necklaces around your neck.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 1:10"/>My child, if sinful people tempt you {to sin with them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">refuse {to do so}.
<verse eid="PRO 1:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 1:11"/>Those sinful people may say, “Join us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We will hide and wait in order to kill someone {who walks by}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, we will hide ourselves in order to suddenly attack an innocent person for no good reason.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 1:12"/>We will kill living people completely, as if we were their grave.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Yes, we will kill} healthy people, as if they could not escape dying.
<verse eid="PRO 1:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 1:13"/>We will discover many valuable treasures!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We will fill our houses with what we steal!
<verse eid="PRO 1:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 1:14"/>Join our gang!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We will share all the loot between us.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 1:15"/>My child, do not associate with those sinful people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Prevent yourself from doing the things that they do!
<verse eid="PRO 1:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 1:16"/>{Avoid those sinners} because they are eager to do wicked things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They even rush to murder people.
<verse eid="PRO 1:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 1:17"/>It is useless {for a hunter} to put out a net {to trap a bird}
</para>
  <para style="q2">while the bird is watching {because the bird will avoid the net}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 1:18"/>However, {these sinful people are more foolish than birds.} They hide in wait, but they kill themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they hide so that they can suddenly attack, but they themselves die.
<verse eid="PRO 1:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 1:19"/>That is what happens to anyone who gains wealth in an unjust manner.
</para>
  <para style="q2">What they gained unjustly will kill them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 1:20"/>Imagine that everything that is wise is a woman who calls out {to everyone} in public.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Imagine that this woman shouts {to people} in crowded places.
<verse eid="PRO 1:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 1:21"/>Imagine that she calls out {to people} at the place where busy streets intersect.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Imagine that she speaks her {wise} words at the {crowded} entrance of the city gates.

<verse eid="PRO 1:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 1:22"/>She says, “You naive people have loved being naive for too long!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You people who ridicule {others} have enjoyed ridiculing {others} to benefit yourselves for too long!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You foolish people have hated what you should know for too long!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 1:23"/>Turn around {and listen} to me when I correct you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Listen! I will tell you all that I am thinking.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, I will help you to understand what I have to say to you.
<verse eid="PRO 1:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 1:24"/>I called out {to you}, but you refused {to listen}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, I invited you to come to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but no one paid any attention {to me}.
<verse eid="PRO 1:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 1:25"/>You ignored everything that I advised you to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, you rejected what I said to correct you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 1:26"/>Therefore, as for me, I will laugh at you when disastrous things happen to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, I will ridicule you when you are terrified.
<verse eid="PRO 1:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 1:27"/>{Yes,} when you are terrified as if a violent storm has arrived,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{when} disastrous things happen to you violently,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} when you become distressed and anguished{, I will ridicule you}!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 1:28"/>At that time, those foolish people will cry out to me {to help them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I will not reply {to them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they will desperately look for me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they will not be able to find me.

<verse eid="PRO 1:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 1:29"/>{Those foolish people will not find me} because they refuse to learn.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Also, they have decided not to respect Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 1:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 1:30"/>Those foolish people rejected what I advised them to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they detested everything I said to correct them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 1:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 1:31"/>Those foolish people will suffer rightly for what they have done.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they will suffer fully for what they have planned.
<verse eid="PRO 1:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 1:32"/>Ultimately, naive people will die because they refuse {to be wise}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being complacent will destroy foolish people.
<verse eid="PRO 1:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 1:33"/>By contrast, people who listen attentively to what I say will live safely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will not fear that something evil might happen to them.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 1:33"/><verse eid="PRO 1:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PRO 2"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 2:1"/>My child, accept what I say.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Consider what I command {you} to be precious.
<verse eid="PRO 2:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 2:2"/>{Do this by} listening carefully to what is wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and by} thinking seriously about what you should understand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 2:3"/>Yes, cry out {to God} for {him to show you} what you should perceive.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Call loudly {to God} for {him to teach you} what you should understand!
<verse eid="PRO 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 2:4"/>Try to learn what is wise as eagerly as you would try to find silver.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, look for it as you would look for a treasure that someone has hidden.
<verse eid="PRO 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 2:5"/>{If you do those things,} then you will understand how to reverently fear Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{If you do those things,} then you will be able to know God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 2:6"/>{This is} because Yahweh provides people with what is wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He tells them what they should know and understand.
<verse eid="PRO 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 2:7"/>He gives what is truly wise to upright people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He protects people who behave honestly.
<verse eid="PRO 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 2:8"/>{He does these things} in order to guard those people who live justly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, he keeps safe those people who are faithful to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 2:9"/>{If you listen to me,} then you will understand what is righteous, just, and honest—
</para>
  <para style="q2">all the best ways to behave.
<verse eid="PRO 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 2:10"/>{This is because} you will truly know what is wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and knowing {what is wise} will please you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 2:11"/>Being able to choose wisely will make you safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being able to understand {what is happening around you} will make you secure.
<verse eid="PRO 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 2:12"/>{Being wise like this} will keep you from doing wicked things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and you will stay away} from people who speak perversely.
<verse eid="PRO 2:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 2:13"/>Those people refuse to behave righteously in order to behave wickedly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 2:14"/>They gladly do what is wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They enjoy doing things that are perverse and evil.
<verse eid="PRO 2:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 2:15"/>They behave deceptively.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they act deviously.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 2:16"/>{Being discreet and insightful} will protect you {also} from adulterous women.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Being discreet and insightful will save you} from immoral women who speak {to you} seductively.
<verse eid="PRO 2:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 2:17"/>Those women left the husbands they married when they were young.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They even forgot what they had promised to God {when they married}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 2:18"/>{Being discreet and insightful will rescue you} because {going to} such a woman’s house will cause you to die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, going with her is the same as going to the place where the spirits of dead people are.

<verse eid="PRO 2:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 2:19"/>No man who acts adulterously with her will live again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will no longer be able to live in a way that results in life with God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 2:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 2:20"/>Therefore, behave like a good person.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, conduct yourself like a righteous person.
<verse eid="PRO 2:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 2:21"/>This is important because {only} people who live uprightly will live in our land,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, it is the people who do not act wickedly who will stay in this land for a long time.
<verse eid="PRO 2:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 2:22"/>By contrast, Yahweh will remove people who act wickedly from our land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be sure of this: Yahweh will completely remove people who act treacherously from this land!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 2:22"/><verse eid="PRO 2:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PRO 3"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 3:1"/>My child, remember the rules I have taught you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Always be mindful to obey what I have commanded you!
<verse eid="PRO 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 3:2"/>{Do this} because {obeying} what I have commanded you will help you live for a long time with many fulfilling and peaceful years.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 3:3"/>Always be faithful and trustworthy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let everyone see {how faithful and trustworthy you are, as if} they were a necklace you are wearing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Remember to be faithful and trustworthy at all times.
<verse eid="PRO 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 3:4"/>As a result of doing so, both God and people will approve of you and consider you an insightful person.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 3:5"/>Trust Yahweh completely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not rely on what you understand.
<verse eid="PRO 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 3:6"/>Let Yahweh lead you whenever you do anything.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As a result {of doing so}, he will show you what you should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 3:7"/>Do not think that you know what is best.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Instead, revere Yahweh and refuse to do what is evil.
<verse eid="PRO 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 3:8"/>Doing so will make your body healthy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {doing so} will strengthen you from the inside.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 3:9"/>Revere Yahweh {by giving to him} some of your riches,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {by giving to him} some of the first {crops} from everything that you harvest.
<verse eid="PRO 3:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 3:10"/>{Doing so} will result in your places for storing crops becoming completely full {of crops}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even your containers for wine will overflow with fresh wine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 3:11"/>My child, do not refuse to listen when Yahweh corrects you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not be resentful even when he rebukes you.
<verse eid="PRO 3:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 3:12"/>{Do not respond in that way} because Yahweh {only} reproves the people whom he loves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as a father reproves the children whom he cherishes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 3:13"/>People who become wise are happy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, the people who understand {Yahweh’s world are the ones who} are truly happy.
<verse eid="PRO 3:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 3:14"/>{This is} because being wise benefits people more than silver {could benefit them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being wise is worth more to people than having gold.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 3:15"/>Being wise is more valuable than precious jewels.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There is nothing that you could desire that is worth as much as being wise.
<verse eid="PRO 3:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 3:16"/>Being wise will help you live for a long time.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Being wise will help you become wealthy and honorable.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 3:17"/>Being wise will allow you to live pleasantly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, in every way being wise will allow you to live peacefully.
<verse eid="PRO 3:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 3:18"/>What is wise is {like} a tree {with fruit} that sustains the people who possess it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">People who are consistently wise live happily.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 3:19"/>Yahweh made the world through being wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Through being skillful, he made the sky and everything in it.
<verse eid="PRO 3:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 3:20"/>Through knowing all things, Yahweh made water burst forth from deep {below the earth} and he made water fall from the clouds {above}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 3:21"/>My child, always remember to do what is prudent and brings a good outcome.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Always be mindful to do those things.
<verse eid="PRO 3:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 3:22"/>Doing so will give you a satisfying life
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people will honor and respect you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 3:23"/>Doing what is prudent and good will {also} cause you to live safely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will keep you from making any serious mistakes.
<verse eid="PRO 3:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 3:24"/>When you lie down {to sleep}, you will not fear anything.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will lie down {to sleep} and sleep peacefully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 3:25"/>Do not worry about something terrible suddenly happening {to you},
</para>
  <para style="q2">or about {what will happen} when God destroys wicked people.
<verse eid="PRO 3:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 3:26"/>{Do not worry} because Yahweh will make you confident.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will not allow people to harm you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 3:27"/>Do not refrain from giving what is good to people who deserve it
</para>
  <para style="q2">when you are able to do so.
<verse eid="PRO 3:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 3:28"/>When you are with a friend {who needs something}, and you have it with you, do not tell that person,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Go away and come back tomorrow. I will give it to you then.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 3:29"/>Do not plan to harm people that you interact with, because they live near you and they trust you.
<verse eid="PRO 3:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 3:30"/>Do not argue needlessly with someone who has not harmed you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 3:31"/>Do not envy violent people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not imitate anything they do.
<verse eid="PRO 3:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 3:32"/>{Do not do so} because Yahweh detests {such} people who act wickedly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he converses like a friend with people who act uprightly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 3:33"/>Yahweh causes bad things to happen to the families of wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he causes good things to happen to the families of righteous people.
<verse eid="PRO 3:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 3:34"/>When people ridicule {others}, it is Yahweh who ridicules them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he kindly helps those who are humble.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 3:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 3:35"/>People will honor wise people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people will shame foolish people.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 3:35"/><verse eid="PRO 3:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PRO 4"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 4:1"/>Children, listen carefully to what I, your father, am teaching you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Pay attention in order to learn what you should understand.
<verse eid="PRO 4:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 4:2"/>{Do this} because what I am teaching you is good.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{So} remember the rules that I am teaching you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 4:3"/>When I was just a boy with my father,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} my mother’s delicate, only son.
<verse eid="PRO 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 4:4"/>During that time, my father taught me. He told me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Remember what I have told you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do what I have commanded you, so that you will keep on living!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 4:5"/>Learn what is wise and what you should understand!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Always remember and keep doing the things that I have said to you!
<verse eid="PRO 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 4:6"/>Keep doing what is wise, because doing so will keep you safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Love doing what is wise, because being wise will protect you from harm.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 4:7"/>Being wise is the most important thing. {So} become wise!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Even if} it costs you everything that you own, become a person who understands {God’s world}!
<verse eid="PRO 4:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 4:8"/>Prize what is wise, so that you will become great.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People will honor you when you value what is wise.
<verse eid="PRO 4:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 4:9"/>Being wise will make you {respectable,} as though you had an attractive wreath on your head.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being wise will make you {honorable,} as though you were wearing a magnificent crown.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 4:10"/>My child, listen attentively and accept what I say.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Doing so will increase the number of years that you live.
<verse eid="PRO 4:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 4:11"/>I instructed you in how to act wisely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I directed you in how to live in the right way.
<verse eid="PRO 4:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 4:12"/>{If you follow my teaching,} nothing will hinder you {from succeeding}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, if you attempt great things, you will do well.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 4:13"/>Consistently remember the things I have instructed you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">keep remembering them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Always be mindful of them, because they will keep you alive.
<verse eid="PRO 4:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 4:14"/>Do not do what wicked people do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, do not behave in the way that evil people behave.
<verse eid="PRO 4:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 4:15"/>Shun doing what is evil. Do not even consider doing it!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Refuse to act wickedly and do something else.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 4:16"/>{Do not act wickedly} because {it is as if} evil people cannot even sleep unless they have done something evil {on that day};
</para>
  <para style="q2">{it is as if} they cannot rest unless they hurt someone.
<verse eid="PRO 4:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 4:17"/>{Do not act wickedly} because evil people do wicked things as if they were eating food;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they violently hurt others as if they were drinking wine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 4:18"/>As for righteous people, they will live {wisely and safely} as people do who walk in the sunshine;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{they will live more and more wisely and safely,} just as the sun shines brighter and brighter until the brightest time of day.
<verse eid="PRO 4:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 4:19"/>{But} the way that wicked people live is {dangerous,} like people {who walk} in total darkness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Like people walking in darkness do not know} what they trip over, wicked people do not know {what hurts them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 4:20"/>My child, pay attention to what I am saying to you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Listen carefully to what I say!
<verse eid="PRO 4:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 4:21"/>Keep thinking about what I say!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Fully commit yourself to remembering such things!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 4:22"/>{Do this} because those who live according to my words will have good lives,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their whole bodies will be healthy.
<verse eid="PRO 4:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 4:23"/>More than anything else, be extremely careful about what you think and desire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because those things will control how you live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 4:24"/>Do not say anything that deceives people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, never say anything that misleads people.
<verse eid="PRO 4:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 4:25"/>{Focus on doing what is right, like} someone who is always looking straight ahead.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {act like} someone who is looking straight in front of himself.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 4:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 4:26"/>Plan carefully to do things in the right way.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As a result {of doing so}, you will succeed in everything that you do.
<verse eid="PRO 4:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 4:27"/>Do not do anything other than what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Prevent yourself from doing what is evil.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 4:27"/><verse eid="PRO 4:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="PRO 5"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 5:1"/>My son, pay attention to the wise things that I tell you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Listen carefully to what I say you should understand!
<verse eid="PRO 5:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 5:2"/>{Do this} so that you will be able to choose wisely {what to do},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {so that} you will know the {right} things to say.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 5:3"/>{Do this} because what adulterous women say seems delightful like the taste of honey.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, their words are more soothing than how olive oil feels on your skin.
<verse eid="PRO 5:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 5:4"/>However, after being with such a woman you will be miserable, as if you had eaten a bitter plant.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{You will suffer} like a person whom someone has cut with a sharp, double-edged sword.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 5:5"/>{Being with} such a woman will cause both of you to die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, what she does {with you} will cause you to become a dead person.
<verse eid="PRO 5:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 5:6"/>She does not want to do what will cause her to live well.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She does not realize that she {lives precariously like someone who} is walking on a broken path.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 5:7"/>So now, children, pay attention to what I say!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Always remember what I have spoken to you!
<verse eid="PRO 5:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 5:8"/>Stay far away from any adulterous woman!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not even go near the door of the place where such a woman dwells!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 5:9"/>If you go to such a woman, you will be giving the best efforts of your youth to others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a merciless person will take away {everything that you would gain in} the best time of your life.
<verse eid="PRO 5:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 5:10"/>If you go to such a woman, people you do not know will satisfy themselves with {what you produced} when you were strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and an outsider will fill his house with what you labored to gain.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 5:11"/>Then you will groan when you are about to die
</para>
  <para style="q2">and have worn out your whole body.
<verse eid="PRO 5:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 5:12"/>Then you will say, “I hated it extremely when people corrected me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, I scorned people when they rebuked me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 5:13"/>I did not obey the people who taught me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, I did not listen carefully to the people who instructed me.
<verse eid="PRO 5:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 5:14"/>My people are close to considering me as someone who has wasted his life.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 5:15"/>{So be like} someone who only drinks water from his own well;
</para>
  <para style="q2">have sex with your wife only.
<verse eid="PRO 5:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 5:16"/>{Do not be like} someone who lets his water run out into the streets;
</para>
  <para style="q2">never have sex with other women!
<verse eid="PRO 5:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 5:17"/>Only have sex with your own wife!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not have sex with other women!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 5:18"/>{As a result,} may Yahweh bless your marriage {with children};
</para>
  <para style="q2">enjoy {sexually} the woman whom you married when you were young!
<verse eid="PRO 5:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 5:19"/>{She is as beautiful as} a loving deer and a graceful mountain goat.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let her breasts satisfy you always.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Constantly be exhilarated by how she loves you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 5:20"/>My son, you should never be exhilarated by an adulterous woman!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You should never passionately caress an immoral woman!
<verse eid="PRO 5:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 5:21"/>{Never do that} because Yahweh fully knows what people do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, he knows everything that people do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 5:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 5:22"/>The wicked things that wicked people do are {like} traps that catch them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the sinful things that they do are {like} ropes by which others can grab them.
<verse eid="PRO 5:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 5:23"/>Those wicked people will die because they did not discipline themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will do what kills them because they are extremely foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 5:23"/><verse eid="PRO 5:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="PRO 6"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 6:1"/>My child, if you guarantee to pay a loan for someone you meet,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{that is, if} you agree to pay a loan for someone you do not know,
<verse eid="PRO 6:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 6:2"/>{if in this way} you have said things that you regret
</para>
  <para style="q2">{because} it would be very difficult for you {to fulfill} what you promised,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 6:3"/>then, my child, do this in order to save yourself {from having to pay back this loan}:
</para>
  <para style="q2">humbly go to that person and beg him {to cancel what you have promised}, because he now controls you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 6:4"/>Do not wait until tomorrow; {go immediately!}
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not allow yourself to rest {until you go and talk to him}.
<verse eid="PRO 6:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 6:5"/>Save yourself {immediately},
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if you were a deer fleeing from a hunter
</para>
  <para style="q2">or a bird fleeing from a trapper.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 6:6"/>You lazy person, learn {something} from {watching} ants!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Consider what ants do so that you can be wise.
<verse eid="PRO 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 6:7"/>Absolutely no one tells ants what to do.
<verse eid="PRO 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 6:8"/>{Nevertheless,} they work hard all during the summer,
</para>
  <para style="q2">gathering and storing food {to eat during the winter}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 6:9"/>{But} you lazy person, stop sleeping!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wake up!
<verse eid="PRO 6:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 6:10"/>{If you say to yourself,} “Let me sleep just a little more!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me lay my hands {across my chest} in order to rest comfortably for a little while longer!”
<verse eid="PRO 6:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 6:11"/>Then {the result of being so lazy will be that} you will become poor and needy
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as surely as if a thief has robbed you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 6:12"/>{I will describe for you what} worthless, sinful people {do. They} constantly deceive people by what they say.
<verse eid="PRO 6:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 6:13"/>They make gestures, such as winking their eyes, signaling with their feet, and pointing their fingers {to communicate their evil plans to their friends}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 6:14"/>They are always thinking perversely while planning how to do evil things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They cause people to argue {with each other}.
<verse eid="PRO 6:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 6:15"/>Because of this, disastrous things will suddenly happen to those people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Someone will destroy them instantly and they will not be able to recover.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 6:16"/>Yahweh absolutely hates six, no, seven things:

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:16"/></para>
  <para style="q3"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 6:17"/>being proud, speaking falsely,
</para>
  <para style="q3">someone murdering a person who has not done anything wrong,
<verse eid="PRO 6:17"/></para>
  <para style="q3"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 6:18"/>someone planning ways to act sinfully,
</para>
  <para style="q3">someone eagerly looking for ways to act wickedly,
<verse eid="PRO 6:18"/></para>
  <para style="q3"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 6:19"/>someone who naturally lies when testifying,
</para>
  <para style="q3">and someone causing members of the same family to argue.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 6:20"/>My child, be mindful to obey what I, your father, have commanded {you}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, obey the rules that your mother has commanded.
<verse eid="PRO 6:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 6:21"/>Remember what we have taught you as if it were always a part of you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {remember these lessons as if} you wore them like a necklace.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 6:22"/>The wise things that we have taught you will help you to know what you should do as you go about each day.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will cause you to be safe when you sleep.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When you wake up {in the morning}, they will be what will continue to instruct you.
<verse eid="PRO 6:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 6:23"/>{This is so} because what I have commanded {you} is {like} a lamp {that shows you your way}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, the rules {we taught you} are {like} a light {to guide you}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When we rebuke you while instructing you, {we do that} so that you can do what will give you a good life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 6:24"/>{We taught you these lessons} in order to prevent you from {going to} wicked women,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and to prevent you} from {believing} the seductive talk of immoral women.
<verse eid="PRO 6:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 6:25"/>Do not think lustfully about her beautiful body.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not let her seduce you by the {flirtatious} way she looks at you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 6:26"/>{Do not do so} because, although having sex with a prostitute may only cost you a cheap meal,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{doing so with} an {adulterous} married woman will cause you to die.
<verse eid="PRO 6:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 6:27"/>A man cannot hold fire against his chest without burning his clothes!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 6:28"/>No one can walk on burning coals without blistering his feet!
<verse eid="PRO 6:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 6:29"/>It is similar with anyone who has sex with another man’s wife.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People will certainly punish anyone who does that.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 6:30"/>People do not resent someone who steals if he only steals {food} because he is hungry.
<verse eid="PRO 6:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 6:31"/>Nevertheless, if people catch thieves, those thieves must pay back seven times {as much as they stole to those from whom they stole}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They may have to give everything that they own {in order to repay what they stole}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 6:32"/>By contrast, a man who acts adulterously with a woman is not thinking.
</para>
  <para style="q2">By doing this, he destroys himself!
<verse eid="PRO 6:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 6:33"/>{The woman’s husband} will injure him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">people will despise him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will always be ashamed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 6:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 6:34"/>{This is so} because the jealous husband will become furious.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will act mercilessly when he revenges himself {on the man who acted adulterously with his wife}.
<verse eid="PRO 6:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 6:35"/>That jealous husband will not accept any money {to stop being furious},
</para>
  <para style="q2">no matter how much money you offer him.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 6:35"/><verse eid="PRO 6:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="PRO 7"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 7:1"/>My son, obey what I have told you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Carefully remember the things that I have commanded you.
<verse eid="PRO 7:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 7:2"/>Do what I have commanded {you}, so that you will live {long and well}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Consider the rules I have taught you to be the most precious things that you possess.
<verse eid="PRO 7:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 7:3"/>Constantly remind yourself of the things that I have commanded you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Memorize them!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 7:4"/>Love what is wise as if it were your sister.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, love what you should understand as if it were a close relative.
<verse eid="PRO 7:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 7:5"/>{Do this} so that you will be able to stay away from adulterous women,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {stay away} from immoral women who speak {to you} seductively.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 7:6"/>{I was} once {standing} near the window {in my house},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I looked down {from above the street} through the shutters on the window.
<verse eid="PRO 7:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 7:7"/>Then I observed {someone} among the naive people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I noticed among the youths a young man who does not think wisely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 7:8"/>He walked down the street near the corner of {the road where} the adulterous woman {dwells}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then he walked on the path toward her house.
<verse eid="PRO 7:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 7:9"/>(It was the time of day when night begins, {and then} it became dark.)

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 7:10"/>Then I saw that an adulterous woman approached the young man.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She was wearing a prostitute’s clothing and intended to deceive {the young man}.
<verse eid="PRO 7:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 7:11"/>(That woman spoke loudly and acted rebelliously.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She never stayed at home.
<verse eid="PRO 7:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 7:12"/>She {often} walked around the streets and public places.
</para>
  <para style="q2">At the corner of any road she waited {for a man whom she could seduce}.)

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 7:13"/>When {she saw the young man}, she firmly took hold of him and kissed him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She shamelessly told {him},
<verse eid="PRO 7:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 7:14"/>“Today {I have meat in my house, because} I sacrificed an animal {in the temple} to promise friendship {with Yahweh}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{In this way} I did what I had vowed to do.
<verse eid="PRO 7:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 7:15"/>So I have come out here to meet you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I have come out} to look everywhere for you, and now I have found you!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 7:16"/>I have covered my bed with expensive Egyptian fabric.
<verse eid="PRO 7:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 7:17"/>I have put pleasant-smelling perfumes on my bed:
</para>
  <para style="q2">myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.
<verse eid="PRO 7:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 7:18"/>Come {with me}! Let us satisfy ourselves sexually all night!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let us enjoy ourselves sexually!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 7:19"/>{Come with me} because my husband is not at home.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He has gone away on a long journey.
<verse eid="PRO 7:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 7:20"/>He filled a bag with money and took it with him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will not return home until the middle of the month.”
<verse eid="PRO 7:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 7:21"/>{Thus} that adulterous woman persuaded the young man by speaking many persuasive things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">by speaking seductively she allured him {into doing what she wanted him to do}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 7:22"/>He quickly followed her {to her home}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He {unknowingly} went to die like an ox going to the place where its owner will kill it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He unknowingly went to die} like a foolish person who lets others lead him by a chain to where they will punish him
<verse eid="PRO 7:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 7:23"/>until {someone kills him by} shooting an arrow into his entrails.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He was as foolish} as a bird flying quickly into a trap.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He did not realize that going with the adulterous woman would cause him to die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 7:24"/>So now, children, listen to what I say!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Carefully pay attention to what I have spoken to you!
<verse eid="PRO 7:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 7:25"/>Do not desire to be with any adulterous woman.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, never go with one of them!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 7:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 7:26"/>{Do not do so} because they have ruined the lives of many men.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It would be difficult to count all of the men that they have caused to die!
<verse eid="PRO 7:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 7:27"/>{Going to} an adulterous woman’s house is like choosing to become a dead person.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Those who enter her bedroom will die as a result.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 7:27"/><verse eid="PRO 7:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="PRO 8"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 8:1"/>Imagine that there is a woman who represents everything that is wise. Surely such a woman calls out {to everyone}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, imagine that this woman represents everything that people should understand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Surely such a woman shouts {these things to people}.
<verse eid="PRO 8:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 8:2"/>Imagine that this woman stands at the highest place next to the crowded crossroads {where everyone can hear her}.
<verse eid="PRO 8:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 8:3"/>Imagine that this woman shouts loudly beside the gates at the entrance to a city.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 8:4"/>{Imagine that she proclaims:} “I am calling out to all of you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am speaking to all people!
<verse eid="PRO 8:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 8:5"/>You naive people must learn to be prudent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You foolish people must learn how to be discerning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 8:6"/>Listen {to what I say}, because I will tell you some excellent things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will speak to you about what is right.
<verse eid="PRO 8:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 8:7"/>{Listen to what I say} because I speak what is true.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I detest speaking what is evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 8:8"/>Everything that I say is honest.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I do not say anything that is false or that deceives {people}.
<verse eid="PRO 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 8:9"/>Everything that I say is plain for people who understand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Everything that I say} is right to people who have become knowledgeable.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 8:10"/>Choose {to learn} what I instruct you instead of silver.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {choose to learn} what you should know instead of the finest gold.
<verse eid="PRO 8:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 8:11"/>{Do this} because being wise is more valuable than having precious jewels.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Being wise is more valuable than anything that you can desire.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 8:12"/>I am what is wise. I am a close relative to what is prudent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I enable people to know how to decide things intelligently.
<verse eid="PRO 8:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 8:13"/>Everyone who reverently fears Yahweh hates what is evil.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I{, what is wise,} hate it when people are proud or arrogant.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I hate it when people act wickedly and when people speak perversely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 8:14"/>I advise people well and enable them to be truly wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am what people need in order to understand how things truly are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I strengthen people.
<verse eid="PRO 8:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 8:15"/>I enable kings to rule {well}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I enable} rulers to make righteous laws.
<verse eid="PRO 8:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 8:16"/>I enable princes and nobles to govern {well}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I enable} every royal official who judges righteously {to do so}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 8:17"/>{I am what is wise, and} I benefit anyone who loves me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Anyone who earnestly tries to become wise will succeed.
<verse eid="PRO 8:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 8:18"/>I enable people to become rich and I cause people to honor those people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I enable people to have} riches that will last and {I enable people to become} righteous.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 8:19"/>What I can give people is more valuable than even the purest gold and the best silver.
<verse eid="PRO 8:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 8:20"/>I {always} do what is righteous and just
<verse eid="PRO 8:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 8:21"/>in order to give property to people who love me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will fill up the places where they store valuable items.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 8:22"/>Yahweh had me{, what is wise,} when he began to create {everything}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Indeed, he had me} before he started doing that.
<verse eid="PRO 8:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 8:23"/>Yahweh established me a very long time ago—at the very beginning, before the world existed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 8:24"/>Yahweh revealed me before the oceans existed
</para>
  <para style="q2">and before there were springs abounding with water.
<verse eid="PRO 8:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 8:25"/>Yahweh revealed me before he made the mountains {and} before {he made} the hills.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 8:26"/>{Yahweh revealed me} before he made the land or the fields or the first particles of dirt on the earth.
<verse eid="PRO 8:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 8:27"/>I was there when Yahweh made the sky,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} when he made the boundary between the sky and the ocean’s surface.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 8:28"/>{I was there} when Yahweh made the clouds above {the earth},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} when he made the springs flow at the bottom of the ocean.
<verse eid="PRO 8:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 8:29"/>{I was there} when Yahweh set boundaries for the seas,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that the water {in the seas} would not go past the boundaries that he commanded.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I was there} when Yahweh made the parts supporting the dry land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 8:30"/>At that time I was {like} someone who was beside Yahweh,
 skillfully helping him to create {everything}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I made him happy every day.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I was always rejoicing when I was with him.
<verse eid="PRO 8:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 8:31"/>{I was} rejoicing in the whole world that Yahweh had made.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I was also happy with the people {he had made}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 8:32"/>So now, children, pay attention to what I say!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Do this} because anyone who obeys my teachings will be happy.
<verse eid="PRO 8:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 8:33"/>Listen to what I teach {you}, so that you will become wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Think about what I teach you!
<verse eid="PRO 8:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 8:34"/>People who listen to me will be happy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People who are as eager to listen to me as if they were waiting {for me} at the door of my house every day
</para>
  <para style="q2">and watching for me to come out {will be happy}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 8:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 8:35"/>{This is true} because people who learn to be wise will live {well},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh will approve of them.
<verse eid="PRO 8:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PRO 8:36"/>But those who refuse to be wise hurt themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All those who hate to be wise {act like they are people who} would love to die.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 8:36"/><verse eid="PRO 8:36"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="PRO 9"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 9:1"/>Continue imagining that there is a woman who represents everything that is wise. Imagine that this woman has built her own {spacious} house
</para>
  <para style="q2">and made seven pillars {to support its roof}.
<verse eid="PRO 9:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 9:2"/>{Imagine that she has prepared a meal for guests.}
</para>
  <para style="q2">She has prepared the meat {to eat} and wine {to drink}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She has {fully} prepared her table for a meal.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 9:3"/>Imagine that this woman has sent out her maids {to invite her dinner guests}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then she calls out at the highest place in the city {where everyone can hear her}.

<verse eid="PRO 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 9:4"/>She tells those who are not wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Come into {my house}, all you naive people!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 9:5"/>Come {to me}! Eat the food that I have prepared,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and drink the wine that I have prepared.
<verse eid="PRO 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 9:6"/>Stop acting naively so that you can live {well}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do what will cause you to learn what you should understand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 9:7"/>If you {try to} teach someone who ridicules {other people}, that person will ridicule you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you correct an evil person, that person will hurt you.
<verse eid="PRO 9:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 9:8"/>{So} do not correct a person who ridicules {other people}. If you do so, then that person will hate you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{However,} if you correct a wise person, that person will love you {for doing so}.
<verse eid="PRO 9:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 9:9"/>If you instruct wise people, then they will become even wiser.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you teach righteous people, then they will learn even more.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 9:10"/>If you want to be wise, you must start by revering Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {only} by knowing what is holy will you understand {which teachings are wise and true}.
<verse eid="PRO 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 9:11"/>Surely being wise will cause you to live for many more years.
<verse eid="PRO 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 9:12"/>Any wise person benefits himself from being wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as anyone who ridicules {other people} will personally suffer for doing so.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 9:13"/>Foolish women speak loudly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">act naively, and are very ignorant.
<verse eid="PRO 9:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 9:14"/>They sit at the doors of the places where they dwell.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They sit} on seats at the highest place in the city {where everyone can hear them}.
<verse eid="PRO 9:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 9:15"/>{They sit there} in order to call out to the people who are walking past them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They call out to} those walking down the road, who are only concerned about where they are going.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 9:16"/>They tell those who are not wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Come into {my house}, all you naive people!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 9:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 9:17"/>{Come to me, because having sex with someone to whom you are not married is} as sweet as water that you have stolen.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {it is} as delicious as food that you eat all by yourself.”
<verse eid="PRO 9:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 9:18"/>But men who go to the houses of such women are not aware that the men who have gone there before have died.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They are not aware} that the guests of such women are now in the deepest parts of the place where dead people are.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 9:18"/><verse eid="PRO 9:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="PRO 10"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 10:1"/>{These are more} wise sayings {said} by Solomon:
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wise children make their fathers glad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish children make their mothers sad.
<verse eid="PRO 10:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 10:2"/>Riches that people acquire by acting wickedly will not benefit them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who act righteously prevent themselves from dying {too soon}.
<verse eid="PRO 10:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 10:3"/>Yahweh prevents righteous people from starving,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he prevents wicked people from getting what they want.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 10:4"/>People who are lazy become poor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who work hard become rich.
<verse eid="PRO 10:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 10:5"/>Sons who collect crops at the right time are insightful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but sons who sleep during the time to harvest crops are shameful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 10:6"/>God blesses righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wicked people say {sometimes} prevents others from knowing about the violent acts {that they do}.
<verse eid="PRO 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 10:7"/>People will be happy when they remember righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people will forget wicked people as if they were something that decays {and disappears}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 10:8"/>People who think wisely are willing to obey the {good} things that people tell them to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who speak foolishly destroy themselves.
<verse eid="PRO 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 10:9"/>People who behave honestly will live safely;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God will catch people who behave deceitfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 10:10"/>People who gesture with their eyes {to deceive others} hurt {people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who speak foolishly destroy themselves.
<verse eid="PRO 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 10:11"/>What righteous people say is like a spring that enables people to live long and well;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wicked people say prevents others from knowing about the violent acts {that they do}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 10:12"/>When people hate others, they argue with each other;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when people love others, they forgive people for the wrong things that they do.
<verse eid="PRO 10:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 10:13"/>Discerning people say what is wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but someone must punish people who do not think wisely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 10:14"/>Wise people continue to learn all that they can,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when foolish people speak, they start to destroy things.
<verse eid="PRO 10:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 10:15"/>What rich people own keeps them safe like a strong wall keeps a city safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but poor people suffer much because they are poor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 10:16"/>God rewards righteous people by allowing them to live {for a long time},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God recompenses wicked people by punishing them for sinning.
<verse eid="PRO 10:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 10:17"/>People who heed what is instructive will live for a long time;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who do not let others correct them do what will destroy them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 10:18"/>People who hate {others} but pretend that they do not {hate them} speak falsely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People who slander others are foolish.
<verse eid="PRO 10:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 10:19"/>People who talk a lot sin a lot;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who refrain from speaking {unnecessarily} are wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 10:20"/>What righteous people say is {as valuable as} the best silver;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} what wicked people think is worthless.
<verse eid="PRO 10:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 10:21"/>What righteous people say benefits many people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people die because they do not think wisely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 10:22"/>When people become wealthy, {it is because} Yahweh has blessed them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and working harder will not make them to become wealthier.
<verse eid="PRO 10:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 10:23"/>Foolish people enjoy doing the wicked things that they planned {to do},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but sensible people enjoy doing what is wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 10:24"/>Wicked people will experience what frightens them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people will receive what they want.
<verse eid="PRO 10:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 10:25"/>When something disastrous happens, it destroys wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people are {like} a foundation that lasts forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 10:26"/>Lazy people irritate people who send them {to do something for them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">like vinegar irritates teeth and smoke irritates eyes.
<verse eid="PRO 10:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 10:27"/>People who revere Yahweh will live for a long time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people will live for only a short time.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 10:28"/>What righteous people hope for will make them joyful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wicked people hope for will not happen.
<verse eid="PRO 10:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 10:29"/>Yahweh protects honest people like a fortress because they live the way that he directs people to live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but not living that way destroys people who act sinfully.
<verse eid="PRO 10:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 10:30"/>Righteous people will always be secure,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people will never live in our land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 10:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 10:31"/>Righteous people say what is wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh will stop people from speaking who speak perversely.
<verse eid="PRO 10:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 10:32"/>Righteous people know good things to say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people {continually} say things that are not true.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 10:32"/><verse eid="PRO 10:32"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="PRO 11"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 11:1"/>Yahweh detests {people} using weighing instruments in order to deceive others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but it pleases him when people use correct weights {on their weighing instruments}.
<verse eid="PRO 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 11:2"/>When people act proudly, they will soon disgrace themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but humble people are wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 11:3"/>Upright people know what to do because they are honest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but being deceitful will ruin treacherous people.
<verse eid="PRO 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 11:4"/>What people own will not help them when Yahweh punishes {wicked people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he will not kill those who live righteously.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 11:5"/>Being righteous will cause innocent people to live securely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but being wicked will ruin those who act wickedly.
<verse eid="PRO 11:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 11:6"/>Being righteous will cause people who act uprightly to escape {harm},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but desiring {bad} things will cause people who act treacherously to trap themselves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 11:7"/>When wicked people die, what they hoped for never happens;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they hoped that being strong would benefit them, but it will not.
<verse eid="PRO 11:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 11:8"/>Yahweh rescues righteous people from becoming distressed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people will become distressed instead.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 11:9"/>People who reject God ruin other people by what they say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what righteous people know will cause them to escape.
<verse eid="PRO 11:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 11:10"/>People in a city rejoice when the righteous people {there} prosper,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they shout joyously when wicked people die.
<verse eid="PRO 11:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 11:11"/>A city becomes great when people who act uprightly bless {the people there},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what people who act wickedly say destroys that city.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 11:12"/>People who {openly} detest someone they know are not thinking wisely;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but understanding people say nothing.
<verse eid="PRO 11:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 11:13"/>People who go around gossiping tell {others} what is secret,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but trustworthy people will keep a matter private.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 11:14"/>Not having anyone to guide a group of people will ruin them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but having many people to advise them will keep that group secure.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 11:15"/>People who guarantee {to pay a debt} for someone they do not know will surely suffer,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who avoid agreeing {to do such a thing} will be safe.
<verse eid="PRO 11:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 11:16"/>People honor a gracious woman,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but cruel men {only} get wealth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 11:17"/>People who are faithfully kind greatly benefit themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but cruel people hurt themselves.
<verse eid="PRO 11:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 11:18"/>People who act wickedly falsely believe that they have gained {something good},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God truly rewards people who do what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 11:19"/>People who truly act righteously will live {well},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who eagerly do what is evil will die.
<verse eid="PRO 11:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 11:20"/>Yahweh detests people who think deceitfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who act blamelessly please him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 11:21"/>It is certain that Yahweh will punish wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that he will not punish those who belong to the righteous group.
<verse eid="PRO 11:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 11:22"/>{It is as unsuitable for} a beautiful woman to refuse to act discreetly
</para>
  <para style="q2">{as it is for} a pig to have a gold ring in its snout.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 11:23"/>When righteous people get what they want, it results in only good things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when wicked people get what they hope for, it results in {Yahweh} being angry.
<verse eid="PRO 11:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 11:24"/>Some people generously share {what they have with others} but they receive even more.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Other people keep more {of what they have} than they should keep, but they still become poor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 11:25"/>People who generously bless others will prosper;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who generously give others what the others need will also receive everything that they need.
<verse eid="PRO 11:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 11:26"/>People curse anyone who {selfishly} hoards grain {instead of selling it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they bless people who sell it {when others need it}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 11:27"/>If you sincerely want to do what is right, people will treat you well,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but evil things happen to people who try to do what is evil.
<verse eid="PRO 11:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 11:28"/>People who depend on their money will not be successful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people will thrive like a green plant.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 11:29"/>People who trouble their families will not inherit anything,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who act foolishly will serve people who think wisely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 11:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 11:30"/>What righteous people say and do is {like} a tree {with fruit} that keeps people alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who persuade others {to be righteous} are wise.
<verse eid="PRO 11:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 11:31"/>Pay attention! Righteous people on the earth will get what they deserve;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but even more so, wicked, sinful people will {also} get what they deserve!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 11:31"/><verse eid="PRO 11:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="PRO 12"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 12:1"/>People who love other people correcting them {also} love {learning} what they should know.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But people who hate other people correcting them are foolish.
<verse eid="PRO 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 12:2"/>Yahweh approves of people who are good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he condemns people who plan to do what is evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 12:3"/>People do not become secure by acting wickedly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people are {as secure as} a tree with immovable roots.
<verse eid="PRO 12:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 12:4"/>A virtuous wife causes people to praise her husband,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but a disgraceful wife {destroys her husband} like a disease that destroys his bones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 12:5"/>Righteous people plan {to treat people} fairly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">wicked people advise {people} in order to deceive {them}.
<verse eid="PRO 12:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 12:6"/>What wicked people say {is like a trap that} kills people {who pass by};
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what upright people say will enable them to escape.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 12:7"/>Yahweh destroys wicked people and they disappear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the families of righteous people will continue.
<verse eid="PRO 12:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 12:8"/>People will praise someone according to how insightful that person is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people will despise someone who thinks perversely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 12:9"/>It is better to be a lowly person yet have a servant
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to think that you are important yet have no food.
<verse eid="PRO 12:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 12:10"/>Righteous people care for their animals,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but even when wicked people {think that they} act compassionately, they act cruelly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 12:11"/>People who work hard will have enough food {to eat},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who waste time doing worthless things do not think wisely.
<verse eid="PRO 12:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 12:12"/>Wicked people want what evil people steal,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people benefit {others} like a tree with deep roots.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 12:13"/>The sinful things that wicked people say will destroy them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people escape from trouble.
<verse eid="PRO 12:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 12:14"/>The {good} things that people say {to others} will {also} satisfy them with what is good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">what people work hard to accomplish will {also} benefit them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 12:15"/>Foolish people {always} think that what they are doing is right;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wise people listen to what other people advise {them to do}.
<verse eid="PRO 12:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 12:16"/>People know immediately when foolish people are angry;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but smart people ignore it when someone disrespects them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 12:17"/>People who naturally say what is true speak righteously,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but witnesses who say what is false speak deceitfully.
<verse eid="PRO 12:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 12:18"/>When people speak without thinking {about what to say}, they hurt others like someone who stabs people with a sword,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wise people say helps people heal.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 12:19"/>What people say truthfully will last forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what people say falsely will {only} last for a moment.
<verse eid="PRO 12:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 12:20"/>People who plan to act evilly think deceitfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who advise others to act peacefully will be joyful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 12:21"/>Bad things {usually} do not happen to righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people will experience many bad things.
<verse eid="PRO 12:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 12:22"/>Yahweh detests people who speak falsely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who act faithfully please him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 12:23"/>Smart people do not reveal {all of} what they know,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people shout out foolish things.
<verse eid="PRO 12:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 12:24"/>People who work hard will reign {over others},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but lazy people will become forced laborers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 12:25"/>When people worry, they feel sad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when others speak kindly to them, it causes them to be cheerful again.
<verse eid="PRO 12:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 12:26"/>Righteous people guide their friends {in the right way to live},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but by living wickedly, wicked people destroy themselves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 12:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 12:27"/>Lazy people do not even cook the animals that they catch,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who work hard value their possessions.
<verse eid="PRO 12:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 12:28"/>People who do what is righteous will live.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, people who do so will not die.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 12:28"/><verse eid="PRO 12:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="PRO 13"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 13:1"/>Wise children pay attention when their fathers instruct them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who ridicule {other people} do not pay attention when people correct {them}.
<verse eid="PRO 13:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 13:2"/>The {good} things that people say are {like} good food to them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the violent things that treacherous people do are {like} food for them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 13:3"/>People who are careful about what they say enable themselves to stay alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} people who speak carelessly destroy themselves.
<verse eid="PRO 13:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 13:4"/>Lazy people want things very much and get very little,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who work hard will receive everything that they want.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 13:5"/>Righteous people detest speaking falsely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wicked people do is disgusting and disgraceful.
<verse eid="PRO 13:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 13:6"/>Acting righteously enables people who act blamelessly to be safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but acting wickedly causes sinful people to do what will destroy them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 13:7"/>Some people act as if they are wealthy while they are {actually} poor.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Other people act as if they are poor while they are {actually} wealthy.
<verse eid="PRO 13:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 13:8"/>Rich people {might} have to pay money {to someone who threatens them} in order to stay alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but poor people do not {even} listen when someone threatens them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 13:9"/>Righteous people live joyfully like a light {that shines brightly},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people {will merely die} like an oil lamp that stops burning {oil}.
<verse eid="PRO 13:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 13:10"/>People who act proudly cause people to argue,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who let others advise them cause people to be wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 13:11"/>Riches that people gain effortlessly will disappear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who gain {riches} by working steadily will increase {their riches}.
<verse eid="PRO 13:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 13:12"/>People despair when they do not receive what they have been hoping to receive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when people receive what they have been wanting to receive, they feel like they have everything that they need.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 13:13"/>People who detest what others {try to} teach them will suffer {for doing so},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God will reward those people who respect what he has commanded.
<verse eid="PRO 13:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 13:14"/>What wise people teach continuously benefits people throughout their lives.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It enables people to avoid dangerous things that could kill them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 13:15"/>People approve of people who are very insightful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but treacherous people are stubborn in the way that they live.
<verse eid="PRO 13:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 13:16"/>All clever people think carefully before they do something,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people show that they are foolish {by how they act}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 13:17"/>Bad things happen to messengers who are not reliable,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but reliable messengers make people peaceful.
<verse eid="PRO 13:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 13:18"/>People who do not let other people correct them will become poor and ashamed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people respect those who let other people rebuke them {for any bad behavior}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 13:19"/>People feel pleasant when they get what they want,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people detest refusing to do what is evil.
<verse eid="PRO 13:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 13:20"/>People who associate with wise people will become wise {themselves},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who are companions of foolish people will suffer.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 13:21"/>Bad things happen to sinful people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but good things happen to righteous people.
<verse eid="PRO 13:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 13:22"/>Good people will leave riches for their grandchildren {when they die},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people will receive the riches that sinful people have saved.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 13:23"/>Poor people have fields that can produce a lot of food,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but unjust people take it away {from them}.
<verse eid="PRO 13:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 13:24"/>Parents who do not punish their children {for bad behavior act as if they} hate their children,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but parents who {truly} love their children are careful to discipline them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 13:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 13:25"/>Righteous people have enough {food} to eat and satisfy themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people will be hungry.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 13:25"/><verse eid="PRO 13:25"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="PRO 14"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 14:1"/>The wisest women help their families to thrive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish women ruin their families by {the foolish} things that they do.
<verse eid="PRO 14:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 14:2"/>People who behave uprightly {show that they} greatly revere Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who behave deceptively {show that they} detest Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 14:3"/>What foolish people say causes others to punish them for being proud,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wise people say protects them.
<verse eid="PRO 14:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 14:4"/>If a man has no oxen {to plow his field}, he does not need to put grain in their feedbox,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but if he has oxen, they will enable {him to produce} an abundant crop.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 14:5"/>Honest witnesses do not lie,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but dishonest witnesses lie easily.
<verse eid="PRO 14:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 14:6"/>People who ridicule {other people} try to become wise and fail to do so,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who understand {what is right} learn things easily.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 14:7"/>If you associate with foolish people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will not learn {anything} from knowledgeable people.
<verse eid="PRO 14:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 14:8"/>People who have good sense know that it is wise to understand {the consequences of} what they do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but stupid people deceive {themselves and others}, which is foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 14:9"/>Foolish people scorn people who make amends with Yahweh after sinning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh approves of people who do what is right.
<verse eid="PRO 14:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 14:10"/>Only you truly know how miserable you are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and only you truly know how joyful you are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 14:11"/>The families of wicked people will die out,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the families of upright people will thrive.
<verse eid="PRO 14:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 14:12"/>There is a way to do things that is easy and convenient for people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but in the end, doing things that way will cause them to die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 14:13"/>People who are laughing may still be suffering,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who feel joyful may ultimately feel sad.
<verse eid="PRO 14:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 14:14"/>People who refuse {to live righteously} will receive {from Yahweh} what they deserve {from living that way};
</para>
  <para style="q2">and good people {will also receive from Yahweh} what they deserve {from living the good way}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 14:15"/>Naive people believe whatever people say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but smart people think carefully about what they do.
<verse eid="PRO 14:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 14:16"/>Wise people are careful and avoid doing things that annoy {others},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people confidently interfere {in other people’s business}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 14:17"/>People who quickly become angry act foolishly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people hate those who plan to do evil things.
<verse eid="PRO 14:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 14:18"/>Naive people only acquire foolish habits,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the reward for clever people is what they know.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 14:19"/>{Some day} evil people will {respectfully} bow in front of good people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wicked people will bow at the doors of {the houses where} righteous people {dwell}.
<verse eid="PRO 14:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 14:20"/>Even the friends of poor people despise them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but rich people have many friends.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 14:21"/>It is sinful to despise your {poor} neighbors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God is pleased with those who do kind things for poor people.
<verse eid="PRO 14:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 14:22"/>People who plan to act wickedly are surely doing the wrong thing with their lives,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who plan to do what is good are faithful and trustworthy people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 14:23"/>If people work hard, they will gain from it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but if people {only} talk, they will remain poor.
<verse eid="PRO 14:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 14:24"/>A reward of being wise is to become rich,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but because stupid people are foolish, they {only} become more foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 14:25"/>Truthful witnesses save people from dying,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but deceptive people tell lies {that cause harm to people}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 14:26"/>People who revere Yahweh are completely confident {that he will protect them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh will also protect their children.
<verse eid="PRO 14:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 14:27"/>Reverently fearing Yahweh is like having a refreshing spring that enables people to live well.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It enables people to avoid what could kill them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 14:28"/>Kings who rule over many people are glorious,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but kings who have no people {to rule over} have nothing.
<verse eid="PRO 14:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 14:29"/>People who do not become angry quickly are very wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who become angry quickly show everyone how foolish they are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 14:30"/>Feeling peaceful makes a person’s body healthy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but envying others {makes a person’s body unhealthy, like something that} rots a person’s bones.
<verse eid="PRO 14:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 14:31"/>People who make poor people suffer ridicule Yahweh, who made them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who are kind to needy people respect Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 14:32"/>Wicked people destroy themselves by doing evil things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people are safe {even} when they die.
<verse eid="PRO 14:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 14:33"/>Understanding people think wisely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when one is among foolish people what is wise is {especially} obvious.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 14:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 14:34"/>Acting righteously makes a country great,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but acting sinfully disgraces communities.
<verse eid="PRO 14:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 14:35"/>Insightful servants please their kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but kings are furious with {servants} who act disgracefully.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 14:35"/><verse eid="PRO 14:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 14"/>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="PRO 15"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 15:1"/>Replying gently to angry people will calm them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but speaking harshly {to them} will make them angrier.
<verse eid="PRO 15:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 15:2"/>What wise people say makes others want to know more,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people constantly say what is foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 15:3"/>Yahweh sees everything that is happening;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he observes both evil people and good people.
<verse eid="PRO 15:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 15:4"/>What people say soothingly is {like} a tree {with fruit} that enables people to live well,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what people say deceitfully makes people despair.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 15:5"/>Foolish people detest what their fathers say to correct them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who let others rebuke them are clever.
<verse eid="PRO 15:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 15:6"/>Righteous people have houses that contain a lot of riches,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what wicked people gain disrupts them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 15:7"/>What wise people say informs others of what they should know,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what foolish people think does not do that.
<verse eid="PRO 15:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 15:8"/>Yahweh detests the sacrifices that wicked people offer {to him},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he delights in the prayers of upright people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 15:9"/>Yahweh detests what wicked people do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he loves people who diligently try to do what is right.
<verse eid="PRO 15:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 15:10"/>Yahweh will severely punish people who refuse to live righteously,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} people who refuse to let other people correct them will perish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 15:11"/>Yahweh knows everything about the place where dead people are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so he surely knows everything that everyone thinks!
<verse eid="PRO 15:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 15:12"/>People who ridicule others despise anyone who corrects them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they avoid wise people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 15:13"/>People smile when they are happy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but feeling sad can make people despair.
<verse eid="PRO 15:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 15:14"/>Sensible people are always trying to learn more,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people satisfy themselves with what is foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 15:15"/>People who suffer experience bad things every day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but cheerful people live as though they are always feasting.
<verse eid="PRO 15:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 15:16"/>Being poor while reverently fearing Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">is better than being rich while worrying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 15:17"/>It is better for someone to have a small meal of vegetables with people who love each other
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to have a large meal of good meat with people who hate each other.
<verse eid="PRO 15:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 15:18"/>People who easily become angry cause people to argue,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who do not easily become angry will help people to be peaceful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 15:19"/>Lazy people are {unproductive} like people walking through thorny plants,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but upright people are {productive} {like people} walking on a level road.
<verse eid="PRO 15:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 15:20"/>Wise sons and daughters make their parents happy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but any sons or daughters who detest their parents are foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 15:21"/>People who are not wise enjoy acting foolishly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but understanding people do what is right.
<verse eid="PRO 15:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 15:22"/>People will not accomplish what they plan to do if there is no one to advise them {well},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when many people advise them {well}, they will succeed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 15:23"/>People rejoice when they answer someone aptly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is so good to say something at the right time!
<verse eid="PRO 15:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 15:24"/>Insightful people live in a way that causes their lives to become increasingly better,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order for them to avoid living in a way that would result in dying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 15:25"/>Yahweh will destroy what proud people own,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he protects the {few} things that widows own.
<verse eid="PRO 15:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 15:26"/>Yahweh detests the evil things that people think,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the pleasing things that people say are pure.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 15:27"/>People who gain wealth in an unjust manner trouble their families,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who refuse bribes will live {in a better way}.
<verse eid="PRO 15:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 15:28"/>Righteous people think carefully about how to reply to people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people quickly say what is evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 15:29"/>Yahweh does not listen to {what} wicked people {request him to do},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he listens {and responds} when righteous people pray {to him}.
<verse eid="PRO 15:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 15:30"/>People feel happy when they see someone smile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} people feel healthy when they hear something good.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 15:31"/>People who begin to behave in a more life-giving way when others rebuke them {for behaving badly} show that they belong to the group of wise people.
<verse eid="PRO 15:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 15:32"/>People who refuse to let others correct them {act as if they} despise themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who listen when others rebuke them think wisely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 15:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 15:33"/>Revering Yahweh teaches people to be wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people must be humble before other people can respect them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 15:33"/><verse eid="PRO 15:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 15"/>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="PRO 16"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 16:1"/>People plan what they want {to say},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh determines how they will {actually} speak.
<verse eid="PRO 16:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 16:2"/>People think that everything that they do is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh knows why people do what they do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 16:3"/>Entrust what you do to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will make what you plan {to do} succeed.
<verse eid="PRO 16:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 16:4"/>When Yahweh made everything, he planned what would happen to each thing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He has even made wicked people for the time when he will punish them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 16:5"/>Yahweh detests all proud people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will certainly punish them.
<verse eid="PRO 16:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 16:6"/>Be loyal to Yahweh and faithfully obey him; if you do that, he will forgive you for having sinned.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People who revere Yahweh will avoid doing what is evil.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 16:7"/>When Yahweh approves of what people do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he even causes their enemies to be peaceful with them.
<verse eid="PRO 16:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 16:8"/>It is better {for someone} to have {just} a few things while being righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">than {for someone} to have a lot of crops while being unjust.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 16:9"/>People plan what they want to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh determines what they will {actually} do.
<verse eid="PRO 16:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 16:10"/>Kings speak for God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when kings judge, they must {always} speak justly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 16:11"/>Yahweh made accurate weighing instruments {for us to use honestly}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, he made all the stones in the {weighing} bag {so that we would use them honestly}.
<verse eid="PRO 16:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 16:12"/>Kings {should} detest any wicked thing that people do
</para>
  <para style="q2">because acting righteously causes kings to rule securely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 16:13"/>{Ideally,} kings enjoy hearing people speak honestly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they love people who say what is true.
<verse eid="PRO 16:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 16:14"/>When kings are angry, they cause people to die,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so wise people will appease them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 16:15"/>When kings are happy, they let people live;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they approve of people, it is as refreshing as rain in springtime.
<verse eid="PRO 16:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 16:16"/>Becoming wise is better than having gold.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, it is better to choose to become understanding than to have silver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 16:17"/>Upright people act in a way that avoids doing what is evil;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who want to stay alive are careful about what they do.
<verse eid="PRO 16:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 16:18"/>Being proud causes people to destroy themselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being arrogant causes people to ruin themselves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 16:19"/>It is better to live humbly among poor people
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to {live proudly and} receive some of what proud people have taken from others.
<verse eid="PRO 16:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 16:20"/>People who act prudently in a matter will succeed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who trust in Yahweh are happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 16:21"/>People will call those who think wisely, “understanding ones,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who speak pleasantly are able to teach others effectively.
<verse eid="PRO 16:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 16:22"/>Being insightful allows a person to live well continually,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people can only teach others to be foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 16:23"/>What wise people think causes them to speak insightfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and what those people say causes others to learn.
<verse eid="PRO 16:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 16:24"/>The pleasing things that people say are {like} a honeycomb:
</para>
  <para style="q2">They cause people to feel pleasant and healthy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 16:25"/>There is a way to do things that is easy and convenient for people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but in the end, doing things that way will cause them to die.
<verse eid="PRO 16:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 16:26"/>Being hungry helps working people work
</para>
  <para style="q2">because wanting to eat motivates people to keep on working.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 16:27"/>Worthless people plot how to hurt others;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the evil things they say harm others like fire burns {people}.
<verse eid="PRO 16:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 16:28"/>Perverse people cause other people to argue with each other,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who gossip about others cause friends to stop being friends.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 16:29"/>Violent people tempt other people {to sin},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they guide them to behave wickedly.
<verse eid="PRO 16:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 16:30"/>People who use their eyes to signal to others are planning to do something perverse;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who use their lips to signal to others are about to do the evil thing {that they had planned to do}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 16:31"/>{The} gray hair {that old people have} is {like} an honorable crown {on their heads};
</para>
  <para style="q2">they achieve it by living righteously.
<verse eid="PRO 16:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 16:32"/>It is better to be someone who does not become angry quickly than to be powerful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is better to control oneself than to be {as powerful as} someone who conquers a city.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 16:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 16:33"/>People throw lots {in order to decide what to do},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh decides whatever happens.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 16:33"/><verse eid="PRO 16:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 16"/>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="PRO 17"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 17:1"/>It is better for someone to have a little stale food {to eat} while living peacefully
</para>
  <para style="q2">than for someone to live in a house where people frequently eat large meals while arguing with each other.
<verse eid="PRO 17:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 17:2"/>An insightful slave will become the boss of a disgraceful son {of his master},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that slave will inherit a portion {of his master’s property} along with his master’s sons.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 17:3"/>People put silver and gold into very hot furnaces {to burn out what is impure},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh tests what people are thinking and desiring to do {in a similar manner}.
<verse eid="PRO 17:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 17:4"/>People who act wickedly listen carefully when people speak what is sinful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who lie pay attention when people say things that destroy {others}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 17:5"/>People who ridicule poor people despise Yahweh, who made them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh will certainly punish people who rejoice when other people experience disastrous things.
<verse eid="PRO 17:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 17:6"/>Old people are proud of their grandchildren,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and children are proud of their parents.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 17:7"/>It is not fitting for worthless people to speak eloquently.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is even less fitting for royal officials to speak falsely!
<verse eid="PRO 17:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 17:8"/>People who pay bribes think that bribes are magical;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{by paying bribes, they think that} everything that they do will be successful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 17:9"/>If you want people to love you, forgive them for the wrong things that they have done to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you continue to remind them about those {wrong} things, they will no longer be your friends.
<verse eid="PRO 17:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 17:10"/>Rebuking sensible people once causes them to learn
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than hitting foolish people a hundred times {causes them to learn}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 17:11"/>Evil people only want to rebel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so a merciless messenger will come and punish them.
<verse eid="PRO 17:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 17:12"/>A mother bear who is furious because someone has stolen her cubs is dangerous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but it can be more dangerous to confront a foolish person who is doing something foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 17:13"/>If someone does bad things to people who have done good things to him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then bad things will always happen to his family.
<verse eid="PRO 17:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 17:14"/>When people start arguing with each other, it is {as difficult to stop as it is to stop} water that is leaking out {of a dam},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so prevent yourself from arguing before you start to argue.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 17:15"/>There are people who acquit guilty people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there are people who condemn innocent people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh detests both types of people.
<verse eid="PRO 17:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 17:16"/>How useless it is for foolish people to try to pay money in order to become wise
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they are unable to think!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 17:17"/>A friend loves {you} all the time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and relatives exist in order to help {other relatives} when disastrous things happen.
<verse eid="PRO 17:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 17:18"/>People who do not think wisely agree to pay someone else’s loan
</para>
  <para style="q2">and even guarantee to pay that loan in front of people whom they know.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 17:19"/>People who love to sin {also} love to cause people to argue;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who brag a lot cause others to destroy them.
<verse eid="PRO 17:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 17:20"/>People who think deceitfully will not experience good things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and bad things will happen to people who speak deceitfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 17:21"/>Foolish people grieve their parents.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, worthless people will cause their parents to be very sad.
<verse eid="PRO 17:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 17:22"/>Being cheerful helps the body to heal,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but being discouraged makes the body weak.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 17:23"/>Wicked people accept bribes that people give to them secretly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they will decide matters unfairly.
<verse eid="PRO 17:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 17:24"/>Understanding people concentrate on what is wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people cannot concentrate on anything.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 17:25"/>Foolish children grieve their fathers
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make their mothers miserable.
<verse eid="PRO 17:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 17:26"/>Punishing innocent people is surely very bad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} flogging noble people {would be just as} wrong.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 17:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 17:27"/>People who refrain from speaking {unnecessarily} are knowledgeable,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who can remain calm are {truly} wise.
<verse eid="PRO 17:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 17:28"/>People will think even foolish people are wise if those foolish people do not speak.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, if fools refrain from speaking people will consider them to be insightful.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 17:28"/><verse eid="PRO 17:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 17"/>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="PRO 18"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 18:1"/>People who avoid other people only care about doing what they want to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They refuse to do anything that is wise.
<verse eid="PRO 18:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 18:2"/>Foolish people hate learning.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Instead, they only want to tell others what they think.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 18:3"/>People treat wicked people contemptuously,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people scold people who act shamefully.
<verse eid="PRO 18:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 18:4"/>What {wise} people say is as profound as a deep ocean.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wise people are {always saying wise things, like} a fountain that flows in a constant stream.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 18:5"/>It is very evil {for judges} to favor guilty people
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to prevent judging innocent people justly.
<verse eid="PRO 18:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 18:6"/>What foolish people say makes people argue,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it makes people want to beat them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 18:7"/>What foolish people say will ruin them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, what they say may cause them to die, as a trap {may cause an animal to die}.
<verse eid="PRO 18:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 18:8"/>People are eager to listen to what people who gossip say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and what they say deeply affects those who hear it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 18:9"/>People who are lazy when they work
</para>
  <para style="q2">are like people who destroy things.
<verse eid="PRO 18:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 18:10"/>Yahweh is {like} a strong tower
</para>
  <para style="q2">that righteous people run into and are safe.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 18:11"/>Rich people think that what they own keeps them safe like walls keep cities safe;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they think that what they own protects them as well as a high wall.
<verse eid="PRO 18:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 18:12"/>Before people ruin themselves, they have first become proud;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and before people will respect someone, that person must become humble.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 18:13"/>It is foolish and shameful
</para>
  <para style="q2">for someone to reply to what a person has said before hearing it.
<verse eid="PRO 18:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 18:14"/>When someone is inwardly strong, he can endure being sick.
</para>
  <para style="q2">However, when someone is inwardly weak and depressed, it is very difficult to make the person feel better!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 18:15"/>Understanding people are always learning more.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, wise people are always trying to learn more.
<verse eid="PRO 18:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 18:16"/>Giving something {to someone} can benefit the one who gives it;
</para>
  <para style="q2">doing so can enable that person to meet important people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 18:17"/>People who state their cases first seem to be right
</para>
  <para style="q2">until people whom they know arrive and question them.
<verse eid="PRO 18:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 18:18"/>Throwing lots {in order to decide something} can make people stop arguing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it can also decide who is right between powerful people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 18:19"/>It is more difficult to reconcile with a relative {whom you have} offended than {to conquer} a fortified city;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when people argue, they avoid each other as if a castle’s strong gate were between them.
<verse eid="PRO 18:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 18:20"/>What people say will satisfy them when they are hungry.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, what people say will satisfy them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 18:21"/>What people say can cause people to die or to remain alive.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So people who are skillful at talking will strongly influence what happens to themselves {and to others}.
<verse eid="PRO 18:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 18:22"/>A man who marries a {good} wife will experience good things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh approves of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 18:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 18:23"/>Poor people plead for others to be merciful {to them}, but rich people reply {to them} rudely.
<verse eid="PRO 18:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 18:24"/>Having companions {who only seem to be true friends} will destroy a person,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but there is a type of friend who loves us and is more loyal than any brother.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 18:24"/><verse eid="PRO 18:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 18"/>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="PRO 19"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 19:1"/>It is better to be poor and behave honestly
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to speak deceitfully and be foolish.
<verse eid="PRO 19:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 19:2"/>Furthermore, it is very bad for people to be enthusiastic {about doing something} while not knowing {anything about it};
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who act hastily do things wrong.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 19:3"/>People who act foolishly destroy themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yet they become furious with Yahweh {and blame him}.
<verse eid="PRO 19:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 19:4"/>Wealthy people {easily} make many friends,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when people become poor, they lose {even} the friends they have.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 19:5"/>Someone will surely punish lying witnesses.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, someone will surely punish people who lie easily.
<verse eid="PRO 19:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 19:6"/>A lot of people want royal officials to favor them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and many people want to be friends with people who give gifts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 19:7"/>All the relatives of poor people despise them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and even their friends avoid them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Although they call out {to them for help}, they do not {respond}.
<verse eid="PRO 19:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 19:8"/>People who love to learn benefit themselves;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who are consistently sensible will surely succeed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 19:9"/>Someone will surely punish lying witnesses.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, people who lie easily will die.
<verse eid="PRO 19:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 19:10"/>It is wrong for foolish people to live luxuriously,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it is even worse for slaves to reign over princes!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 19:11"/>Insightful people do not get angry quickly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people show how honorable they are by forgiving {people who} sin {against them}.
<verse eid="PRO 19:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 19:12"/>When kings are furious, they frighten people like the roaring of young lions {frightens people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when they approve of people, it is as refreshing {for the people} as dew {is} on plants.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 19:13"/>Foolish children destroy their fathers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when wives argue {with their husbands}, it is {as annoying as} constantly dripping water.
<verse eid="PRO 19:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 19:14"/>People inherit houses and riches from their fathers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh {alone} gives {men} insightful wives.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 19:15"/>Lazy people sleep well,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but {such} idle people are {always} hungry.
<verse eid="PRO 19:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 19:16"/>People who obey {God’s} commandments stay alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who do not care about {God’s} ways will die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 19:17"/>Giving things to poor people is {like} loaning them to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will reward anyone who does this.
<verse eid="PRO 19:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 19:18"/>Discipline your children while {they are young and} you can expect them to learn {to live in the right way}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{If you} do not {discipline them}, {it is as though you} want them to die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 19:19"/>Very angry people will pay {for being angry};
</para>
  <para style="q2">so if you rescue them {once from what they must pay}, you will have to do that again and again.
<verse eid="PRO 19:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 19:20"/>Pay attention to what people advise you {to do} and let people teach you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do so, you will become wise for the rest of your life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 19:21"/>People plan to do many things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but {only} what Yahweh advises will succeed.
<verse eid="PRO 19:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 19:22"/>People want others to consider them to be faithful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is better to be poor than to be someone who lies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 19:23"/>Revering Yahweh causes people to live for a long time;
</para>
  <para style="q2">such people rest contentedly at night;
</para>
  <para style="q2">nothing will harm them.
<verse eid="PRO 19:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 19:24"/>Some people are so lazy that even though they have put their hands in a dish {of food},
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will not even lift the food to their mouths.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 19:25"/>{If you} punish people who ridicule {others},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{then} naive people {who see you do that} will learn to be sensible.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{If you} correct understanding people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{then} they will know even more.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 19:26"/>Children who act violently toward their fathers and chase away their mothers
</para>
  <para style="q2">are disgraceful and embarrassing.
<verse eid="PRO 19:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 19:27"/>My child, if you want to become stupid,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then stop listening to what people teach you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 19:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 19:28"/>Worthless witnesses scorn what is just,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wicked people enjoy acting sinfully as if they were gulping down delicious food.
<verse eid="PRO 19:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 19:29"/>Yahweh is ready to condemn people who ridicule {others},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he is ready to beat fools on their backs.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 19:29"/><verse eid="PRO 19:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 19"/>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="PRO 20"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 20:1"/>Drinking a lot of intoxicating drink causes people to start ridiculing and fighting others;
</para>
  <para style="q2">becoming drunk is very foolish.
<verse eid="PRO 20:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 20:2"/>When kings are terrifyingly angry, they frighten people like the roaring of young lions {frightens people};
</para>
  <para style="q2">people who make kings angry cause themselves to die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 20:3"/>It is honorable to cease arguing with other people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but all foolish people are eager to argue with others.
<verse eid="PRO 20:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 20:4"/>Lazy farmers do not plow {their fields} when they should {plow their fields}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then when it is time to harvest {crops}, they look {for crops in their fields}, but there are none.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 20:5"/>Knowing what people are thinking and planning is {as difficult as} drawing water out of a deep {well},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but discerning people are able to do so.
<verse eid="PRO 20:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 20:6"/>Many people claim that they are faithful individuals,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but very few people {actually} act faithfully!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 20:7"/>Righteous people live honestly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their children are very fortunate.
<verse eid="PRO 20:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 20:8"/>{Ideally,} kings who sit on their thrones in order to judge {people}
</para>
  <para style="q2">discern anything that is evil and remove it {from their lands}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 20:9"/>No one can truthfully say, “I do not think sinfully anymore; I do not sin anymore.”
<verse eid="PRO 20:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 20:10"/>Yahweh detests {people dishonestly using} both weights that differ and measurements that differ {to benefit themselves}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 20:11"/>Even young people show others {who they are} by what they do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">how they act shows whether they are innocent and right {or not}.
<verse eid="PRO 20:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 20:12"/>Yahweh has made both ears with which to hear and eyes with which to see.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 20:13"/>If you sleep a lot, you will become poor;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} if you stay awake {and work}, you will have plenty of food.
<verse eid="PRO 20:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 20:14"/>Buyers claim that something is not good at all {when they are bargaining with the seller about its price}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But {after they buy it,} they go and boast {to their friends about the good thing that they bought}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 20:15"/>Gold and precious jewels are plentiful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the knowledgeable things that people say are rare and precious.
<verse eid="PRO 20:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 20:16"/>Take the coats of people who promise to pay a loan for someone whom they do not know.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, hold onto the coats of people who do so for a foreigner {because those people are not likely to repay those loans}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 20:17"/>Food that people get by deceiving {others} may taste sweet {to them at first},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but later what they have done will be {as unpleasant to them as having} a mouth full of rocks.
<verse eid="PRO 20:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 20:18"/>When people give you good advice, {if you do what they suggest,} your plans will succeed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Therefore, let others advise you before you start fighting a war.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 20:19"/>People who walk around gossiping tell {others} what is secret,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so avoid people who speak carelessly.
<verse eid="PRO 20:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 20:20"/>People who curse their parents
</para>
  <para style="q2">{will die like} an oil lamp that stops burning {oil} in a totally dark place.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 20:21"/>If people inherit {property} hastily before the proper time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will ultimately not receive any blessing from it.
<verse eid="PRO 20:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 20:22"/>Do not say that you will harm someone who has harmed you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rather, wait for Yahweh {to resolve the matter}, so that he may vindicate you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 20:23"/>Yahweh detests {people dishonestly using} differing weights {to benefit themselves}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {using} weighing instruments in order to deceive {others} is very bad.
<verse eid="PRO 20:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 20:24"/>Yahweh directs what happens {even} to powerful people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So then, no one can comprehend what will happen to him!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 20:25"/>It is dangerous for people to declare thoughtlessly that they will dedicate something to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then later regret that they have promised to do that.
<verse eid="PRO 20:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 20:26"/>Wise kings separate the wicked people from the good people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then punish the wicked people severely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 20:27"/>Just as the light of a lamp penetrates into and illuminates a dark place, the life-breath that Yahweh puts into each person penetrates into the person’s inner being.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That breath is like the presence of Yahweh, who sees everything that is inside a person.
<verse eid="PRO 20:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 20:28"/>Being faithful and trustworthy makes kings safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being faithful enables them to rule securely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 20:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 20:29"/>People admire young men because they are strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people admire old men because they have become wise.
<verse eid="PRO 20:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 20:30"/>Flogging people for doing evil things can stop them from doing those evil things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and hitting those people {on the outside} can change who they are on the inside.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 20:30"/><verse eid="PRO 20:30"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 20"/>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="PRO 21"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 21:1"/>Yahweh directs what kings think as {a farmer directs} streams of water
</para>
  <para style="q2">to make them go wherever he wants {them to go}.
<verse eid="PRO 21:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 21:2"/>People always think that what they do is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh {rightly} evaluates why they do those things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 21:3"/>Doing what is right and fair is more acceptable to Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">than sacrificing {animals to him}.
<verse eid="PRO 21:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 21:4"/>Being proud and arrogant guide what wicked people do like a lamp {shows people where to go};
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are sinful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 21:5"/>What diligent people plan will certainly profit them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but all those who act too hastily will certainly become poor.
<verse eid="PRO 21:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 21:6"/>When people gain wealth by speaking falsely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that wealth quickly vanishes like mist, {and doing that} will kill them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 21:7"/>When wicked people act violently, they cause others to punish them for it
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they refuse to do what is right.
<verse eid="PRO 21:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 21:8"/>Guilty people continually do what is wrong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but innocent people do what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 21:9"/>It is better to live {alone} in a corner of a housetop
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to live inside a house with a wife who always argues {with you}.
<verse eid="PRO 21:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 21:10"/>Wicked people strongly desire to do what is evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will not be merciful to the people around them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 21:11"/>If you punish people who ridicule others, {then} naive people {who see you do that} will become wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and if you teach wise people, they will become {even more} knowledgeable.
<verse eid="PRO 21:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 21:12"/>Righteous people are able to understand what the households of wicked people do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they let the evil things that wicked people do happen to them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 21:13"/>People who refuse to listen to poor people when they cry out {for help}
</para>
  <para style="q2">will also cry out {for help themselves}, but no one will help them.
<verse eid="PRO 21:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 21:14"/>Secretly giving something to an angry person will stop him from being angry.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, secretly bribing a furious person will calm him down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 21:15"/>Righteous people are glad when people judge justly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but judging justly terrifies people who act sinfully.
<verse eid="PRO 21:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 21:16"/>People who stop behaving sensibly
</para>
  <para style="q2">will {soon} go to the place where the spirits of dead people are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 21:17"/>People who love what is pleasurable will be poor.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, people who indulge themselves in wine and rich food will never be wealthy.
<verse eid="PRO 21:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 21:18"/>Wicked people will suffer instead of righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and treacherous people {will suffer} in place of upright people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 21:19"/>It is better to live {alone} in a desolate land
</para>
  <para style="q2">than {to live} with an argumentative and nagging wife.
<verse eid="PRO 21:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 21:20"/>Wise people store up precious riches and olive oil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but foolish people waste everything that they have.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 21:21"/>People who diligently try to be righteous and faithful
</para>
  <para style="q2">will live {well}, will be righteous, and people will respect them.
<verse eid="PRO 21:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 21:22"/>Wise people know how to conquer cities that mighty warriors are defending;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they can pull down the walls that people {in those cities} believe will protect them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 21:23"/>People who are careful about what they say
</para>
  <para style="q2">avoid becoming distressed.
<verse eid="PRO 21:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 21:24"/>People who ridicule others are proud and arrogant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they behave furiously and presumptuously.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 21:25"/>Lazy people want {food}, but they will die
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they refuse to work.
<verse eid="PRO 21:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 21:26"/>Lazy people always want more things for themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people generously give {what they have to others}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 21:27"/>{Yahweh} detests the sacrifices that wicked people offer {to him};
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is even more {detestable} when they are offering something {to Yahweh} while intending to act wickedly!
<verse eid="PRO 21:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 21:28"/>Witnesses who lie will die,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when someone who listens carefully speaks, what he says will finish the matter.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 21:29"/>Wicked people pretend to know what they are doing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but upright people think about what they do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 21:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 21:30"/>Even the wisest and most knowledgeable counselor is nothing compared to Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 21:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 21:31"/>Soldiers prepare to fight,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh determines who wins {that fight}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 21:31"/><verse eid="PRO 21:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 21"/>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="PRO 22"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 22:1"/>Being someone whom people respect is more important than being very wealthy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, being someone whom others approve of is better than having silver and gold.
<verse eid="PRO 22:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 22:2"/>Rich people and poor people have this in common:
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh made all of them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 22:3"/>Sensible people observe something dangerous happening and avoid it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but naive people just keep going and suffer {for doing so}.
<verse eid="PRO 22:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 22:4"/>People who are humble, who revere Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will become rich, people will respect them, and they will live {long and well}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 22:5"/>Deceptive people live {dangerously,} as if they were walking down a road covered with thorns and traps,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} people who want to stay alive avoid living that way.
<verse eid="PRO 22:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 22:6"/>Teach children how to behave {properly},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that when they become old, they will still continue to do so.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 22:7"/>Rich people reign over poor people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who borrow {money} from others become like slaves to the people who loaned them {money}.
<verse eid="PRO 22:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 22:8"/>People who act unjustly will suffer for doing so,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will no longer be able to furiously oppress other people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 22:9"/>Yahweh will bless generous people
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they give some of their own food to poor people.
<verse eid="PRO 22:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 22:10"/>If you banish people who ridicule others, then people will stop arguing {with each other},
</para>
  <para style="q2">condemning {each other}, and shaming {each other}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 22:11"/>People who love being sincere and
</para>
  <para style="q2">speaking graciously are companions of kings.
<verse eid="PRO 22:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 22:12"/>Yahweh preserves true sayings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he makes what treacherous people say fail.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 22:13"/>Lazy people {as an excuse to not work} claim that there is a lion outside that will kill them in the street {if they go outside}.
<verse eid="PRO 22:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 22:14"/>What adulterous women say is {as dangerous as} a deep hole {that men could fall into};
</para>
  <para style="q2">those with whom Yahweh is angry will suffer from it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 22:15"/>Children naturally think foolishly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but physically disciplining them will teach them to stop being foolish.
<verse eid="PRO 22:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 22:16"/>People who oppress poor people in order to make more money for themselves
</para>
  <para style="q2">or who give things to rich people {in order to become rich} will only become poor.

<verse eid="PRO 22:16"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 22:17"/>Listen carefully to what wise people have said;
</para>
  <para style="q2">consider carefully what I am teaching you!
<verse eid="PRO 22:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 22:18"/>{Do this} because if you remember these sayings
</para>
  <para style="q2">and if you are always ready to repeat them {to others},
</para>
  <para style="q2">then you will be glad.
<verse eid="PRO 22:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 22:19"/>I am teaching these sayings to you—yes, you—right now
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that you will trust Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 22:20"/>I am indeed writing these 30 sayings
</para>
  <para style="q2">to advise and teach you.
<verse eid="PRO 22:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 22:21"/>{I am writing them} in order to teach you what is true in trustworthy sayings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in order to answer those who sent you with trustworthy sayings.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 22:22"/>Do not steal from poor people just because they are poor;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not oppress suffering people in court.
<verse eid="PRO 22:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 22:23"/>{Do not do these things} because Yahweh will defend those poor people when you dispute with them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will kill the people who stole from them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 22:24"/>Do not become friends with angry people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, do not associate with people who easily become angry.
<verse eid="PRO 22:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 22:25"/>{If you do so,} then you will act like them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you will endanger yourself like an animal caught in a trap.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 22:26"/>Stay away from those people who agree to pay loans for others.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Indeed, stay away from those people} who guarantee to pay the loans of others.
<verse eid="PRO 22:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 22:27"/>{Because} if you cannot pay back {the loan},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{then} the person to whom you owe money will surely take away even your own bed {in order to pay back the loan}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 22:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 22:28"/>Do not cheat people by moving the stones that their ancestors placed long ago
</para>
  <para style="q2">to mark the boundaries of their land.
<verse eid="PRO 22:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 22:29"/>Consider this: People who work skillfully will serve kings
</para>
  <para style="q2">rather than serving unknown people.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 22:29"/><verse eid="PRO 22:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 22"/>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="PRO 23"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 23:1"/>When you sit down to eat {a meal} with someone who rules over others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">pay attention to the food that is in front of you.
<verse eid="PRO 23:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 23:2"/>Restrain yourself {from eating too much}
</para>
  <para style="q2">if you like eating a lot of food.
<verse eid="PRO 23:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 23:3"/>Do not crave the {expensive} food that the ruler has
</para>
  <para style="q2">because that ruler is using that food to deceive you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 23:4"/>Do not work so much that you exhaust yourself in order to become rich.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be understanding enough to stop doing so.
<verse eid="PRO 23:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 23:5"/>As soon as you look at that wealth, it will surely be gone!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{This is} because wealth certainly disappears quickly as if it had wings
</para>
  <para style="q2">and flew off into the sky like a fast bird.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 23:6"/>Do not eat food that stingy people {give you}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not crave the expensive food that they have,
<verse eid="PRO 23:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 23:7"/>because stingy people are always thinking about how much the food costs them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will tell you to eat and drink,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they do not mean what they say.
<verse eid="PRO 23:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 23:8"/>{When you realize this,} you will want to vomit what little food you ate.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will have wasted the kind things you said {to them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 23:9"/>Do not {try to} talk to foolish people
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they will {only} despise the insightful things that you say.
<verse eid="PRO 23:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 23:10"/>Do not cheat people by moving the old stones that mark the boundaries of their land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not claim the land that belongs to {defenseless} orphans,
<verse eid="PRO 23:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 23:11"/>because {Yahweh is} the one who redeems them {and he} is powerful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who will defend them when they dispute with you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 23:12"/>Consider carefully {what people say} when they correct you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, listen carefully to what people teach you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 23:13"/>Do not refuse to discipline your children.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you physically punish them, they will not die.
<verse eid="PRO 23:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 23:14"/>In fact, if you physically punish your children,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will prevent them from dying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 23:15"/>My child, if you are wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then surely I myself will be very happy,
<verse eid="PRO 23:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 23:16"/>and I will be deeply joyful
</para>
  <para style="q2">when you say what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 23:17"/>Do not envy sinful people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">instead always revere Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 23:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 23:18"/>{If you do so, then} you will surely have a {good} future,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and what you hope will happen will indeed occur!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 23:19"/>My child, listen {to me} so that you can become wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make yourself think about behaving rightly.
<verse eid="PRO 23:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 23:20"/>Stay away from drunkards and gluttons,
<verse eid="PRO 23:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 23:21"/>because drunkards and gluttons will become poor.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They sleep so much that they will only have rags to wear.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 23:22"/>Pay attention to your father, who enabled you to exist,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and continue to honor your mother when she becomes old.
<verse eid="PRO 23:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 23:23"/>Learn what is true and remember it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Learn what is wise and instructive and what you should understand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 23:24"/>Fathers of righteous people are very joyful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, those who father wise people are happy because of them.
<verse eid="PRO 23:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 23:25"/>So do what will make your parents happy!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do what will make your mother joyful!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 23:26"/>My son, pay close attention to me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Carefully observe what I do!
<verse eid="PRO 23:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 23:27"/>{Do this} because prostitutes are as dangerous as a deep hole.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, {becoming involved with} an adulterous woman is as dangerous as {falling into} a well that you cannot escape from.
<verse eid="PRO 23:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 23:28"/>These very women certainly wait {for men to seduce} like robbers {wait for people to rob}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They cause many men to become unfaithful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 23:29"/>These are the kind of people who are woeful, sorrowful, and quarrelsome,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who lament, get hurt for no reason,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and have red eyes:
<verse eid="PRO 23:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 23:30"/>those people who drink too much wine
</para>
  <para style="q2">and are always looking around for wine {to drink} that someone has prepared.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 23:31"/>Do not let wine become overly attractive to you, even though it is beautifully red, glistens in the cup,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and goes down your throat smoothly.
<verse eid="PRO 23:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 23:32"/>Afterward you will feel as terrible as if a poisonous snake has bitten you.
<verse eid="PRO 23:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 23:33"/>{When you are drunk,} you will hallucinate,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you will imagine distorted things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 23:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 23:34"/>You will feel {dizzy and sick} as if you were trying to sleep on a ship that the sea was tossing back and forth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, you will feel as if you were trying to sleep while swaying at the top of a ship’s sails.
<verse eid="PRO 23:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 23:35"/>{You will say,} “People hit me, but it did not hurt.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People beat me, but I did not feel it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I wish I could be sober
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I could find even more wine {to drink} again!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 23:35"/><verse eid="PRO 23:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 23"/>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="PRO 24"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 24:1"/>Do not envy evil people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not want to associate with them,
<verse eid="PRO 24:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 24:2"/>because they plan to act violently,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they talk about doing bad things to people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 24:3"/>People build households by acting wisely;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they make those households stable by acting sensibly.
<verse eid="PRO 24:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 24:4"/>By acting knowledgeably, people fill the rooms {of those households}
</para>
  <para style="q2">with all kinds of valuable and delightful riches.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 24:5"/>Wise people are strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and knowledgeable people make themselves more powerful,
<verse eid="PRO 24:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 24:6"/>because letting people advise you will make you fight your war successfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and letting many people counsel you will rescue you {from losing the war}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 24:7"/>Foolish people cannot understand what is wise;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have nothing {useful} to say in court.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 24:8"/>{Some} people are always planning to do evil things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people refer to them as schemers.
<verse eid="PRO 24:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 24:9"/>Foolish plans are sinful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people detest those who ridicule others.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 24:10"/>If you give up during distressful times,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then you are weak.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 24:11"/>Save people whom others are trying to kill;
</para>
  <para style="q2">save the ones who will certainly die unless you do something!
<verse eid="PRO 24:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 24:12"/>If you {falsely} claim that you did not know that those people were dying unjustly, then think about this:
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh knows exactly what you are thinking and he understands {what you are doing}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who keeps you alive and he knows {everything about you}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will surely make people receive what they deserve for whatever they have done or not done!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 24:13"/>My child, eat honey because it tastes good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and honey dripping from the comb tastes sweet.
<verse eid="PRO 24:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 24:14"/>Be aware that what is wise is like honey for you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you become wise, then you will have a {good} future,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and what you hope will happen will indeed occur!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 24:15"/>Do not be like wicked people and hide in wait in order to attack the places where righteous people dwell.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not devastate the places where righteous people rest!
<verse eid="PRO 24:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 24:16"/>{Do not do so} because righteous people can recover many times when disastrous things happen to them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but disastrous things will destroy wicked people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 24:17"/>Do not be happy when something disastrous happens to your adversaries.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, do not rejoice when that happens!
<verse eid="PRO 24:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 24:18"/>If you do, then Yahweh will notice and disapprove,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that he stops being angry with your enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 24:19"/>Do not worry about people who do what is evil.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not be envious of wicked people.
<verse eid="PRO 24:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 24:20"/>{Do not do so} because evil people will not have {good} futures,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} wicked people {will merely die} like an oil lamp that stops burning {oil}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 24:21"/>My child, reverently fear Yahweh and kings.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Avoid people who rebel {against either Yahweh or the king},
<verse eid="PRO 24:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 24:22"/>because disastrous things will happen quickly to those people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no one knows how terribly both Yahweh and kings can destroy {others}!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:22"/><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 24:23"/>Here are more things that wise people have said:
</para>
  <para style="q1">It is very evil to favor someone when you judge.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 24:24"/>If anyone declares that a guilty person is innocent,
</para>
  <para style="q2">many people will curse him and whole people groups will hate him.
<verse eid="PRO 24:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 24:25"/>However, people who condemn {guilty people} will prosper,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh will bless them well.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 24:26"/>People who answer honestly show that they are true friends.
<verse eid="PRO 24:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 24:27"/>Do the work you must do outside and prepare your fields
</para>
  <para style="q2">before you build your house.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 24:28"/>Do not testify against someone if you do not have a good reason {to do so},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not try to deceive people by what you say.
<verse eid="PRO 24:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 24:29"/>Do not say, “I will do to him that same {bad} thing that he did to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will pay him back for what he did to me!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 24:30"/>I walked by the land of a lazy person
</para>
  <para style="q2">and past the vineyard of someone who does not think wisely.
<verse eid="PRO 24:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 24:31"/>And I saw that thistles and weeds were everywhere in that field and vineyard. Even the stone wall surrounding them had fallen down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 24:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 24:32"/>When I saw {that}, I considered carefully {what I was seeing}. When I observed {that}, I learned {this}:
<verse eid="PRO 24:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 24:33"/>{If you say to yourself,} “Let me sleep just a little more!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let me lay my hands {across my chest} in order to rest comfortably for a little while longer!”
<verse eid="PRO 24:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 24:34"/>Then {the result of being so lazy will be that} you will become poor and needy
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as surely as if a thief has robbed you.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 24:34"/><verse eid="PRO 24:34"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 24"/>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="PRO 25"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 25:1"/>Here are more wise sayings said by Solomon that the scribes who served Hezekiah, the king of Judah, copied {from a scroll that Solomon had written}:
<verse eid="PRO 25:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 25:2"/>God shows how glorious he is when he makes something that is difficult for people to understand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But kings show how glorious they are when they explain something {that is difficult for people to understand}.
<verse eid="PRO 25:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 25:3"/>As people cannot fully understand how high the sky is or how deep the earth is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so they cannot fully understand what kings think.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 25:4"/>People who make things from metal must remove impurities from silver
</para>
  <para style="q2">before they can make {that silver into} something useful.
<verse eid="PRO 25:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 25:5"/>{In the same way,} people must remove wicked advisers from the presence of kings
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they can rule securely by being righteous.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 25:6"/>Do not promote yourself in front of kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not pretend to be great.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 25:7"/>{Do not do so} because it is better if someone invites you to sit in a place that is closer {to the king},
</para>
  <para style="q2">than for someone to embarrass you in front of a royal official whom you have seen {by telling you to sit farther away from the king}.
<verse eid="PRO 25:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 25:8"/>Do not plead your case too quickly against someone you know.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do, then you will not know what to do when that person {wins the case and} embarrasses you!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 25:9"/>If you do indeed plead your case against someone you know,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{settle it between yourselves and} do not tell {others} any secret about that person.
<verse eid="PRO 25:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 25:10"/>If you do {tell a secret}, then the people who hear you may shame you {for it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people will speak badly about you from then on.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 25:11"/>When someone says something that is very appropriate to a situation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is {as delightful as seeing} golden apples in a setting of silver.
<verse eid="PRO 25:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 25:12"/>When a wise person rebukes someone who is willing to listen,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is {as valuable as} a gold ring or jewelry made from the best gold.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 25:13"/>Reliable messengers are {as refreshing} to those who send them as cold snow would be {refreshing} during the {summer} harvest time;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they refresh the people whom they serve.
<verse eid="PRO 25:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 25:14"/>People who brag about giving something but then do not give it
</para>
  <para style="q2">are as disappointing as clouds and wind that do not bring rain.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 25:15"/>People can persuade leaders by being patient,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by speaking gently people can convince those who oppose them {to agree with them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 25:16"/>If you discover some wild honey, do not eat too much of it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do, then you will become sick from it and vomit.
<verse eid="PRO 25:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 25:17"/>{In the same way,} do not visit too often the houses of your friends.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do, then they may feel that they have had too much of you and {even} hate you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 25:18"/>People who lie when they testify against other people
</para>
  <para style="q2">are {deadly, as if they had attacked them with} a club, a sword, or a piercing arrow.
<verse eid="PRO 25:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 25:19"/>Trusting treacherous people during distressful times
</para>
  <para style="q2">is {like trying to eat with} a rotten tooth or {trying to walk with} a crippled foot.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 25:20"/>Singing songs to someone who is sad
</para>
  <para style="q2">is {as unhelpful as} taking a coat off of someone in cold weather
</para>
  <para style="q2">or pouring vinegar on soda.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 25:21"/>Feed your enemies if they are hungry;
</para>
  <para style="q2">give them something to drink if they are thirsty.
<verse eid="PRO 25:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 25:22"/>{Do so} because by doing so you {will shame them, as if you} were pouring burning coals on top of them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh will reward you {for doing so}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 25:23"/>When wind blows from the north, that produces rain.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Similarly,} when people tell the secrets {of others}, {that produces} angry people.
<verse eid="PRO 25:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 25:24"/>It is better to live {alone} in a corner of a housetop
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to live inside a house with a wife who always argues {with you}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 25:25"/>When people hear something good from a faraway place,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is as {refreshing as drinking} cold water when one is thirsty.
<verse eid="PRO 25:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 25:26"/>When righteous people yield to wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is {as bad as} a spring that people have made murky by walking in it or {as bad as} a polluted fountain.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 25:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 25:27"/>{As} it is not good to eat too much honey;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{so it is not} honorable to try to make people honor you.
<verse eid="PRO 25:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 25:28"/>People who cannot control themselves
</para>
  <para style="q2">are {as defenseless as} a city that an army has broken into and knocked down its walls.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 25:28"/><verse eid="PRO 25:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 25"/>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="PRO 26"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 26:1"/>Honoring foolish people is just as inappropriate
</para>
  <para style="q2">as snow {falling} in {hot} summer and rain {falling} during the time to harvest crops.
<verse eid="PRO 26:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 26:2"/>Just as a bird will fly by {and not land on you},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so a curse will not harm you if you are innocent.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 26:3"/>As people must whip horses and bridle donkeys {in order to guide them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so people must physically punish foolish people {in order to guide them}.
<verse eid="PRO 26:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 26:4"/>Do not reply to foolish people according to their foolish way of thinking.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do, then you also will be foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 26:5"/>Reply to foolish people according to their foolish way of thinking.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do not, then they may think that they are wise.
<verse eid="PRO 26:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 26:6"/>Anyone who asks a foolish person to take a message to someone
</para>
  <para style="q2">is {doing something as foolish as} cutting off his own feet or drinking poison.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 26:7"/>{As} the legs of people who cannot walk are useless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so are the sayings that foolish people say.
<verse eid="PRO 26:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 26:8"/>Honoring foolish people is just {as useless}
</para>
  <para style="q2">as a harmless weapon.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 26:9"/>A drunken person picks up a thorn {and it will hurt someone},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{in the same way} a foolish person says a proverb {that can only be harmful}.
<verse eid="PRO 26:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 26:10"/>People who employ foolish people or random strangers are {as dangerous}
</para>
  <para style="q2">as someone who randomly shoots arrows at people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 26:11"/>Foolish people who do the same foolish thing over and over again
</para>
  <para style="q2">are like dogs that eat what they have vomited up.
<verse eid="PRO 26:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 26:12"/>Consider this: Foolish people are more likely to learn
</para>
  <para style="q2">than people who {wrongly} think that they are {already} wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 26:13"/>Lazy people claim that there is a lion in the path
</para>
  <para style="q2">or in the midst of the streets {so that they can stay inside their houses and do nothing}.
<verse eid="PRO 26:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 26:14"/>As doors swing on their hinges {and do not go anywhere},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so lazy people turn back and forth in their beds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 26:15"/>Lazy people put their hands in a dish {of food},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} they are so lazy that they will not lift the food to their mouths.
<verse eid="PRO 26:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 26:16"/>A {typical} lazy person {wrongly} thinks that he is wiser
</para>
  <para style="q2">than several people who answer intelligently.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 26:17"/>People who make themselves angry because of an argument that does not concern them
</para>
  <para style="q2">are {as foolish as} people who grab the ears of a dog that is passing by.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18-19" style="v" sid="PRO 26:18-19"/>People who trick others
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then say that they were just joking are {as dangerous}
</para>
  <para style="q2">as a crazy person who shoots deadly flaming arrows {at people}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:18-19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 26:20"/>Fires stop burning when they have nothing {to burn}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the same way, people stop arguing when no one is gossiping.

<verse eid="PRO 26:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 26:21"/>{As} charcoal keeps coals burning and wood keeps fires burning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so people who always argue keep other people arguing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 26:22"/>People are eager to listen to what people who gossip say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and what they say deeply affects those who hear it.
<verse eid="PRO 26:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 26:23"/>People who fervently say {that they are your friend} while thinking about doing evil things {to you}
</para>
  <para style="q2">{are as deceptive as} a {cheap} clay pot that someone has made to look like silver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 26:24"/>People who hate you will use what they say to hide what they feel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they are {really} thinking about how to betray you.
<verse eid="PRO 26:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 26:25"/>Do not believe those people when they speak kindly to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they are thinking many detestable things.
<verse eid="PRO 26:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 26:26"/>Although those people deceive others by pretending that they do not hate you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">When people gather together, they will discover how wicked those people are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 26:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 26:27"/>People who dig pits to trap others will fall into those pits instead;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who try to crush others with stones will become crushed by those stones instead.
<verse eid="PRO 26:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 26:28"/>Liars hate the people whom they hurt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and flatterers cause disastrous things to happen.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 26:28"/><verse eid="PRO 26:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 26"/>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="PRO 27"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 27:1"/>Do not brag about {what you will do} tomorrow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you do not know what will happen then.
<verse eid="PRO 27:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 27:2"/>Do not praise yourself; let someone else praise you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, let other people praise you, not yourself.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 27:3"/>Stones and sand are heavy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but fools are so annoying that they are harder to bear than either of those.
<verse eid="PRO 27:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 27:4"/>Angry people are cruel and furious people are destructive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but no one can withstand jealous people!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 27:5"/>It is better to correct people openly, than to love them without showing them that you love them.
<verse eid="PRO 27:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 27:6"/>Friends will be faithful to you by criticizing you {when necessary},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but enemies will deceive you by acting affectionately toward you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 27:7"/>When people have full stomachs, they do not want to eat {even} honey.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But when people are hungry, {even} bitter things taste sweet to them.
<verse eid="PRO 27:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 27:8"/>People who stray from their homes
</para>
  <para style="q2">are like birds that stray from their nests.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 27:9"/>Fragrant oil and perfume make people feel happy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but having a friend who advises you sincerely is even better.
<verse eid="PRO 27:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 27:10"/>Do not ignore your friends or your father’s friends.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not {think that you must} go to the house of a relative when something disastrous happens to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Rather,} it is better to go to a nearby neighbor than to relatives who live far away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 27:11"/>My child, make me happy by becoming wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then I will be able to reply to anyone who argues against me.
<verse eid="PRO 27:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 27:12"/>Sensible people observe something dangerous happening and avoid it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but naive people {ignorantly} do not avoid it and suffer {for doing so}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 27:13"/>Take the coats of people who promise to pay a loan for someone whom they do not know.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, hold onto the coats of people who do so for a foreigner.
<verse eid="PRO 27:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 27:14"/>If you rise early in the morning and loudly call out a blessing to your neighbor {while he is still sleeping}, he will consider it to be a curse{, not a blessing}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 27:15"/>A wife who always argues {with you} is as {annoying as}
</para>
  <para style="q2">constantly dripping water on a rainy day.
<verse eid="PRO 27:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 27:16"/>It is as difficult to stop her {from arguing} as stopping the wind,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or catching oil in one hand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 27:17"/>{We can use} one iron tool to sharpen another iron tool;
{similarly,} when one person shares what he is thinking, it can help another person to think more clearly.
<verse eid="PRO 27:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 27:18"/>Just as people who take care of fruit trees will also eat the fruit from those trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so too will masters honor their servants who guard them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 27:19"/>When people look in water, the water reflects their faces.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the same way, what people think reveals what kinds of people they are.
<verse eid="PRO 27:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 27:20"/>Just as the place where dead people go never becomes full;
</para>
  <para style="q2">so people never stop wanting {things}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 27:21"/>People use crucibles and furnaces to test and refine silver and gold.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the same way, people can know what kind of person someone is {by how he reacts} when people praise him.
<verse eid="PRO 27:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 27:22"/>If you were to crush a fool the way that you would crush grain {into powder},
</para>
  <para style="q2">you would still not be able to find any part of him that is not foolish.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 27:23"/>Be fully aware of how your sheep are doing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, consider carefully how your animals fare.
<verse eid="PRO 27:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 27:24"/>{Do so} because riches will not last forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even a king’s family will not rule forever!
<verse eid="PRO 27:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 27:25"/>Harvest the grass and then you will see new grass.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Collect {and store} the plants that grow on the hillside.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 27:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 27:26"/>{If you do these things, then} you will have lambs with wool that you can clothe yourself with. You will also have male goats that you can sell for enough money to buy a field.
<verse eid="PRO 27:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 27:27"/>You will even have female goats that produce enough milk for yourself, your family,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your servant girls to drink.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 27:27"/><verse eid="PRO 27:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 27"/>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="PRO 28"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 28:1"/>Wicked people run away even though no one is chasing them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people are as brave as lions.
<verse eid="PRO 28:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 28:2"/>When the people in a country sin, they will continually have {new} leaders;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when they have a truly knowledgeable ruler, then they will have a {stable} government that will last.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 28:3"/>A poor person who oppresses other poor people
</para>
  <para style="q2">is {as destructive as} rain that washes away {the crops}, leaving nothing to eat.
<verse eid="PRO 28:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 28:4"/>People who reject {Yahweh’s} laws say good things about wicked people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who obey those laws oppose such wicked people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 28:5"/>Evil people cannot comprehend what is just,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who desire to please Yahweh comprehend everything {about it}.
<verse eid="PRO 28:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 28:6"/>It is better to be poor and honest
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to be dishonest and rich.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 28:7"/>Young people who obey {Yahweh’s} laws are wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but young people who carouse with gluttons disgrace their fathers.
<verse eid="PRO 28:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 28:8"/>Money that people gain by charging an unreasonably large amount of interest {from those to whom they loan money}
</para>
  <para style="q2">will {eventually} belong to someone who is kind to poor people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 28:9"/>Yahweh detests hearing prayers from people
</para>
  <para style="q2">who refuse to obey his laws.
<verse eid="PRO 28:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 28:10"/>People who guide upright people to act evilly
</para>
  <para style="q2">will destroy themselves by what they do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people whom Yahweh does not blame {for acting wickedly} will receive what is good.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 28:11"/>Rich people tend to think that they are wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but perceptive poor people can tell whether or not this is true.
<verse eid="PRO 28:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 28:12"/>People celebrate when righteous people become powerful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people hide when wicked people become powerful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 28:13"/>People who {try to} hide the sinful things that they do will never be successful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh will be merciful to people who confess the sinful things that they have done and stop doing them.
<verse eid="PRO 28:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 28:14"/>People who constantly examine how they are thinking and behaving are happy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but bad things will happen to people who become uncaring about those things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 28:15"/>Wicked people who rule over poor people are {as dangerous as}
</para>
  <para style="q2">a roaring lion or attacking bear.
<verse eid="PRO 28:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 28:16"/>Leaders who are not sensible severely oppress {other people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} people who despise gaining wealth unjustly will live for a long time.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 28:17"/>People who murder others will keep running away {from those who would punish them} until they die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not help them!
<verse eid="PRO 28:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 28:18"/>Yahweh will rescue people who continually do what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who behave dishonestly will ruin themselves in the end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 28:19"/>People who work hard will have enough food {to eat},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who waste time doing worthless things will only be poor.
<verse eid="PRO 28:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 28:20"/>Yahweh abundantly blesses faithful people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he will certainly punish people who are eager to be wealthy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 28:21"/>Although it is very evil to unfairly favor one person over another,
</para>
  <para style="q2">some people will sin {by doing so} to get even a small bribe.
<verse eid="PRO 28:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 28:22"/>People who are eager to become rich are greedy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do not realize that they will become poor.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 28:23"/>Afterward, people appreciate someone who has corrected them
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than {they appreciate} someone who has spoken flatteringly {to them}.
<verse eid="PRO 28:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 28:24"/>People who rob their parents and say that doing so is not wrong
</para>
  <para style="q2">are as bad as thieves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 28:25"/>Greedy people cause people to argue with each other,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh will prosper people who trust him.
<verse eid="PRO 28:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 28:26"/>People who trust in themselves are foolish,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who act wisely are the ones who will escape {what is dangerous}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 28:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 28:27"/>People who give poor people {what they need} will have all that they need,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but there are many who will curse people who ignore poor people.
<verse eid="PRO 28:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 28:28"/>People hide when wicked people become powerful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but when those wicked people die, there will be more and more righteous people.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 28:28"/><verse eid="PRO 28:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 28"/>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" sid="PRO 29"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 29:1"/>Some people remain stubborn even though other people often correct them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but someday something will destroy them quickly, and they will not be able to recover.
<verse eid="PRO 29:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 29:2"/>People are joyful when righteous people become influential,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people are miserable when wicked people rule {over them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 29:3"/>People who cherish what is wise make their fathers happy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who have sex with prostitutes waste all their money.
<verse eid="PRO 29:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 29:4"/>Kings make the people in their land succeed by acting justly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but leaders who take money dishonestly ruin the people in their land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 29:5"/>People who flatter others
</para>
  <para style="q2">are really just preparing to exploit them in some way
<verse eid="PRO 29:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 29:6"/>Evil people endanger themselves by acting sinfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people sing joyfully and are happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 29:7"/>Righteous people know that they should treat poor people justly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people do not {even} understand that they should know {this}.
<verse eid="PRO 29:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 29:8"/>People who mock others agitate people throughout a city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wise people enable others to remain calm.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 29:9"/>If wise people dispute with foolish people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the foolish people will become angry and sneer and not resolve anything.
<verse eid="PRO 29:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 29:10"/>Murderers despise people who always try to do what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but righteous people try to protect them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 29:11"/>Foolish people uncontrollably express everything that they feel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wise people control how they express what they feel.
<verse eid="PRO 29:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 29:12"/>Leaders who believe the false things that people tell them
</para>
  <para style="q2">have only wicked servants.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 29:13"/>Poor people and the people who oppress {them} have {at least} one thing in common:
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh is the one who causes both of them to live.
<verse eid="PRO 29:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 29:14"/>Kings who judge poor people according to what is true
</para>
  <para style="q2">will always rule securely.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 29:15"/>If parents punish and correct their children, doing so can make those children wise;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but if parents let their children do whatever they want to do, then their children will disgrace them.
<verse eid="PRO 29:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 29:16"/>People sin more when wicked people rule over them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but {someday} Yahweh will destroy those wicked people, and righteous people will see it happen.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 29:17"/>If you discipline your children, then you will no longer feel worried {about their behavior}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will make you very happy.
<verse eid="PRO 29:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 29:18"/>When the people {of a nation} do not have messages from Yahweh {through his prophets}, then they do not control themselves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who obey {Yahweh’s} laws are happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 29:19"/>You cannot correct servants by {only} speaking to them
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they will not do what you say even though they understand {what you say}.
<verse eid="PRO 29:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 29:20"/>Consider this: Foolish people are more likely to do well in life
</para>
  <para style="q2">than people who speak thoughtlessly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 29:21"/>If you give your servants everything they want when they are young,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then they will eventually be arrogant.
<verse eid="PRO 29:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 29:22"/>People who easily become angry cause people to argue.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, angry people cause many people to sin.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 29:23"/>People will humiliate proud people for being proud,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people will honor those who are humble.
<verse eid="PRO 29:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 29:24"/>People who take a share of a thief’s spoils greatly endanger themselves;
</para>
  <para style="q2">They hear that Yahweh will curse them {for not testifying to what they know}, but they do not say anything {about the crime}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 29:25"/>Being anxious is {as dangerous as walking into} a trap,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh will protect people who trust in him.
<verse eid="PRO 29:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 29:26"/>Many {people} want leaders to help them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh is the {only} one who {surely} does for them what is just.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 29:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 29:27"/>Righteous people detest unjust people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wicked people detest people who do the right thing.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 29:27"/><verse eid="PRO 29:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 29"/>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" sid="PRO 30"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 30:1"/>{These are} the sayings of Agur son of Jakeh, which Yahweh told him to say;
</para>
  <para style="q1">{these are what} Agur declared to both Ithiel and Ucal:
<verse eid="PRO 30:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 30:2"/>I am certainly less intelligent than other people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, I do not understand as much as everyone else understands!
<verse eid="PRO 30:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 30:3"/>I have not learned how to become wise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">nor do I know {much} about {Yahweh,} the Holy One.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 30:4"/>{But I will say this:} Surely nobody has ever gone to heaven and returned to earth!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Surely nobody has ever controlled the wind!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Surely nobody has ever gathered the water for rain in the clouds!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Surely nobody has ever formed the boundaries of the earth!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You do not know the name of any such person, or the name of his son.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Therefore, you {also} do not know {much}!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 30:5"/>Everything that God says is true;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is {like} a shield that protects people who trust him to protect them.
<verse eid="PRO 30:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 30:6"/>Never claim that God has said something other than what he has {actually} said.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do that, then he will correct you and he will prove that you lied {about what he said}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 30:7"/>{God,} I ask you to do two things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please do them for me before I die:
<verse eid="PRO 30:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 30:8"/>{Please} prevent me from being dishonest or speaking what is not true.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Please} do not let me become too poor or too rich,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but} just provide the proper amount of food for me.
<verse eid="PRO 30:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 30:9"/>Because if I become rich, I might say that I do not know you and that I do not need you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and if I become poor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I might dishonor you by stealing things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 30:10"/>Never say bad things about servants to the people whom they serve.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do, then they will curse you, and people will hold you responsible {for what you said}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 30:11"/>Some people disrespect their parents.
<verse eid="PRO 30:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 30:12"/>Some people think that they are sinless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they have committed disgusting sins, {like} people who have covered themselves with excrement.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 30:13"/>Some people are very proud!
</para>
  <para style="q1">They think that they are better than other people.
<verse eid="PRO 30:13"/><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 30:14"/>Some people are very cruel toward others;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they harshly oppress and destroy poor people
</para>
  <para style="q1">as fierce animals attack and eat other animals.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 30:15"/>{Greedy people are like} the offspring of leeches
</para>
  <para style="q2">{because they} always want other people to give them more.
</para>
  <para style="q1">There are three, even four things that always want more:
<verse eid="PRO 30:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 30:16"/>the place where dead people are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">childless women,
</para>
  <para style="q2">soil that never receives enough water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and fire that keeps consuming more.
<verse eid="PRO 30:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 30:17"/>People who ridicule their fathers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and refuse to obey their mothers
</para>
  <para style="q1">deserve to {die
</para>
  <para style="q2">and} have wild animals eat their {dead} bodies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 30:18"/>There are three, even four things, that are too amazing for me to comprehend:
<verse eid="PRO 30:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 30:19"/>how a bird flies in the air,
</para>
  <para style="q1">how a snake slithers over a rock,
</para>
  <para style="q1">how a ship sails in the middle of the ocean,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and how a young man loves a young woman.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 30:20"/>Acting adulterously is {as easy} for adulterous women as
</para>
  <para style="q2">eating and wiping their mouths.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Afterward, they claim that they have not sinned at all.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 30:21"/>There are three, even four, things that {the people in} the world cannot tolerate:
<verse eid="PRO 30:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 30:22"/>what slaves do who become rulers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">what worthless people do when they have plenty of food to eat,
<verse eid="PRO 30:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 30:23"/>what women whom people hate do when they marry someone,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and what servant girls do who replace the wives of their masters.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 30:24"/>There are four creatures in the world that are small
</para>
  <para style="q2">but extremely wise:
<verse eid="PRO 30:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 30:25"/>Although ants are not strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they store up their food during the summer {so that they have it to eat during the winter}.
<verse eid="PRO 30:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 30:26"/>Although hyraxes are {also} not strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are able to make their homes {high up in the rocks} on cliffs.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 30:27"/>Although locusts do not have a king,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they move in orderly groups like soldiers in an army.
<verse eid="PRO 30:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 30:28"/>Although anyone can {easily} catch lizards in his hands,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they can freely enter into kings’ palaces.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 30:29"/>There are three, even four, things that look very impressive when they walk:
<verse eid="PRO 30:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 30:30"/>lions, which are the most powerful animals
</para>
  <para style="q2">and never flee from anything,
<verse eid="PRO 30:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 30:31"/>strutting male birds, male goats,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and kings whom people are afraid to rebel against.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 30:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 30:32"/>If you have acted foolishly by bragging about yourself,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or if you were plotting {to do what is evil},
</para>
  <para style="q2">then stop doing so immediately!
<verse eid="PRO 30:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 30:33"/>{Stop doing so} because just as churning milk produces butter,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and squeezing a nose produces blood,
</para>
  <para style="q2">making people angry causes them to fight.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PRO 30:33"/><verse eid="PRO 30:33"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 30"/>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" sid="PRO 31"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 31:1"/>{These are} the sayings of King Lemuel; Yahweh had spoken these sayings that his mother had taught him:
<verse eid="PRO 31:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 31:2"/>My son, whom I gave birth to
</para>
  <para style="q2">and whom I vowed {to dedicate to Yahweh}, listen to me!
<verse eid="PRO 31:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 31:3"/>Do not exhaust yourself by having sex with women;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they can destroy kings.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 31:4"/>Lemuel, kings and dignitaries should not {constantly} drink wine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or {greatly} desire to drink what can intoxicate {them}.
<verse eid="PRO 31:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 31:5"/>{They must not do this} so that they do not forget the laws {that they have made}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and prevent all suffering people from getting what they legally deserve.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 31:6"/>Let dying people drink what can intoxicate {them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let miserable people drink wine.
<verse eid="PRO 31:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 31:7"/>They can drink {what can intoxicate them} to forget that they are poor
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to completely forget what troubles them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 31:8"/>Defend those who cannot speak {for themselves};
</para>
  <para style="q2">{defend} all those whom others are threatening to kill so that they get what they legally deserve.
<verse eid="PRO 31:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 31:9"/>Defend, judge rightly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and plead for suffering and poor people to get what they legally deserve.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 31:10"/>Virtuous and capable women are difficult to find!
</para>
  <para style="q2">This kind of woman is more valuable than precious jewels.
<verse eid="PRO 31:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 31:11"/>Her husband completely trusts her,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will always gain many things {because of her}.
<verse eid="PRO 31:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 31:12"/>Such a woman benefits her husband
</para>
  <para style="q2">for as long as she lives.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 31:13"/>She gets materials to make clothing for both warm and cool weather,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and she enjoys making that clothing.
<verse eid="PRO 31:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 31:14"/>She is like merchant ships
</para>
  <para style="q2">because she brings food to her home from distant places.
<verse eid="PRO 31:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 31:15"/>She gets up before dawn in order to prepare food for her family
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to prepare some {food} for her female servants.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 31:16"/>She carefully evaluates a field and then buys it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Then} she uses some of what she earned by working to plant a vineyard {in it}.
<verse eid="PRO 31:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 31:17"/>She keeps her body strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and she makes her arms strong {by working hard}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 31:18"/>She knows that what she does is very profitable.
</para>
  <para style="q1">She works late into the night.
<verse eid="PRO 31:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 31:19"/>She makes thread {for clothing} with her own hands.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 31:20"/>She generously helps people who are poor and suffering.
<verse eid="PRO 31:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 31:21"/>She is not worried that her family will be cold during cold weather
</para>
  <para style="q2">because her whole family has the best clothing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 31:22"/>She makes her own blankets to cover beds.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She wears clothing made from expensive cloth.
<verse eid="PRO 31:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 31:23"/>People respect such a woman’s husband at the {city} gates,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when he sits {there} with the {other} leaders of the city.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 31:24"/>This woman makes clothing and sells it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">She also sells belts to merchants.
<verse eid="PRO 31:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 31:25"/>People notice how strong and dignified she is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and she is cheerful about what will happen in the future.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 31:26"/>She speaks wisely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when she speaks, she teaches {others} to be faithful and kind.
<verse eid="PRO 31:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 31:27"/>She carefully watches what happens in her household,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and she is never lazy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 31:28"/>This woman’s children stand respectfully and declare that she lives well.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Her husband says good things about her, as well.
<verse eid="PRO 31:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 31:29"/>He says to her, “Many women have acted virtuously and capably,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you indeed have done better than them all!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PRO 31:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 31:30"/>Charming women {who are not good} can deceive people into thinking that they are good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and beautiful women will be beautiful for only a short time.
</para>
  <para style="q2">However, people will {always} praise those women who reverently fear Yahweh.
<verse eid="PRO 31:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 31:31"/>Give to such women what they have earned,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and praise them publicly for what they have done.
<verse eid="PRO 31:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PRO 31"/>
</usx>
